{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla","id":1483112,"title":"Powerful Methuselah or Antedilluvian Imposing his will on Camarilla?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-05T02:13:32-07:00","id":1483112,"title":"Powerful Methuselah or Antedilluvian Imposing his will on Camarilla?","content":"So, what is your take if a powerful Methuselah or Antediluvian awoke and decided to impose his will on the camarilla saying he wants to command the sect, otherwise he's going to force his will or cause havoc in the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T02:24:47-07:00","id":1483113,"title":"","content":"I mean, this is a thought I believe has passed in everyone's mind at least once, once we know the scale of godlike powers they have. In any case, I'm asking more out of curiosity as something similar happened in BJD, with Artemis Orthia appearing before the Inner Concil of the Camarilla and telling them what to do, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T06:37:00-07:00","id":1483122,"title":"","content":"I don't know how well that would work. The Camarilla is, for the most part, a pretty loose organization with the specific goal of preventing the mortal world from finding out vampires exist. It also exists as a forum for vampires to exchange favors and prestige. Individual Princes mostly run their own domains. You do have Justicars and Archons but for the most part, they only intervene when the Masquerade is threatened or when non-Camarilla vampires (like the Sabbat) get up to shenanigans. Overall, the Camarilla is a surprisingly &quot;hands-off&quot; organization.<br /> <br /> If a Methuselah or Antediluvian decided to try and bully the Inner Council into doing what it wants, I don't know how much of an effect that would end up having on the Camarilla on the whole. Like, if the Inner Council/Camarilla suddenly tried to start inserting itself more into local politics and making demands that Princes start engaging in some new activity or whatever, you'd see blowback and possibly rebellions from Princes. For the most part, Princes happy to be a part of the Camarilla because it increases their power, but they're not interested in being puppets to the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> So any Antediluvian or Methuselah would quickly run into the problem that, even if they could control the Inner Circle, that doesn't necessarily equate toexerting much power over the Princes and cities of the Camarilla. Ultimately the Inner Circle just doesn't have the manpower to <i>force</i> the Princes of the world to go along with their demands.<br /> <br /> So I think if something like this did happen, you'd see the Inner Council resorting to soft power, using bribes, blackmail and favors to convince Princes to implement this new paradigm. But at the same time, if Princes feel those plans and goals from the Inner Council are too confining or taking things in a direction they don't like, then those Princes will just say no thank you and if the Inner Council keeps pushing too hard to make Princes do things they don't want to do, you'd likely start seeing cities defect to the Anarchs or a full scale civil war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T09:28:42-07:00","id":1483139,"title":"","content":"The Inner Circle of the Camarilla has as its members some of the most powerful active vampires. There's a reason the game has kept that more or less secret while giving us the names and even stats of the Justicars. We know that some cities' Princes and Primogen have been extremely powerful and ancient themselves, so the Inner Circle is likely to be at least as old and powerful as people like Khalid, Inyanga, Critias, and Mithras. (Or if not, it's because they are doing the bidding of vampires who are.)<br /> <br /> Any attempt to directly intimidate or force them will meet with huge resistance. Not only by the Inner Circle and their small army of Justicars and Archons, but also some of the Gehenna cults and many other elders. It will put a huge target on their back.<br /> <br /> That's why such ancient and powerful vampires typically choose to act more subtly through pawns or front organizations. Almost assuredly there are Methusalehs and Antedeluvians manipulating the Camarilla as a whole. It's less efficient, but far more safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T10:09:53-07:00","id":1483149,"title":"","content":"Are you implying that they don't already do that? Or that the Camarilla wasn't build By the Methusela and Antes that aren't big fans of this new-fangled anarch revolt or sabbat or whatever the neonates are calling it this century.<br /> <br /> The camarilla is already a massive ponzi scheme as is, I don't think anyone would even Notice a change in leadership especially when we consider things like elder+ levels of obfucate. The Ventrue Ante could have been awake the entire time and personally(or at least using Dominate 10: &quot;You are now part of my Character Sheet&quot;) leading the Cammies for all we know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 06-05-2022, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T10:10:14-07:00","id":1483150,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be surprised if mithras has been trying fr centuries. He's definitely powerful for a 4th gen and has a rivalry with hardenstat. <br /> <br /> I guess the ventrue anti could have success because of his mastery of dominate and nobody would know what's happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T10:45:06-07:00","id":1483155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla#post1483112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what is your take if a powerful Methuselah or Antediluvian awoke and decided to impose his will on the camarilla saying he wants to command the sect, otherwise he's going to force his will or cause havoc in the world?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The original Inner Circle members were all &quot;youngsters&quot; when it comes to Methuselahs or Ancients of the &quot;old world&quot;<br /> The Brujah Adana di Sforza was Embraced as a 5th generation vampire by Losario in 1093 CE<br /> The Gangrel Milov Petrenkov was Embraced as a 6th generation vampire by <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Scendrak</span></span></span> in 974 CE (and died probably in 1495)<br /> The Malkavian Camilla Banes was Embraced as a 6th generation vampire by Mellandis in 1063 CE<br /> The Nosferatu Josef von Bauren was Embraced as a 6th generation vampire by an unknown Sire in 1006 CE<br /> The Toreador Rafael de Corazon was Embraced as a 5th generation vampire by Callisti y Castillo in 1182 CE<br /> The Tremere Mistress Fanchon was Embraced as a 6th generation vampire by Shavrael in 1357 CE<br /> The Ventrue Hardestadt (the Elder) was Embraced as a 5th generation vampire by an unknown Sire in 947 CE (weird, a Ventrue who can't trace his liniage back to the antediluvian or on of his 4th gen children...) and Presumably bit the dust in 1395 CE and was replaced by Hardestadt (the Younger) who himself was Embraced in 1191 CE who acted as if he was his Sire<br /> <br /> You see, the Camarilla was founded in 1435 CE<br /> Wich means, this new &quot;fad&quot; of the vampires was made by Vampires whe not even passed their 5th century.<br /> laughable in the eyes of such ancient mostorsities who were VERY active that time like Mithras, Menele, Critias, Helena, Shalmath, Montano, Ankla Hotep, Erik Eigermann or Neferu just to name a few...<br /> Back then if powerful Methuselah or Antediluvian, or even their sire would have awoke to impose his will on the young camarilla? They Inner circle would probably politely asked, whats thy bidding my master?<br /> Today?<br /> The camarilla still not celebrated it's 600th birthday, and we don't exactly know who is in the Inner Circle at the 21th century... but even if the originals remained in charge? A bunch of mostly 6th generation &quot;elders'&quot; who are barely thousand years old I highly doubt would have stand ANY chance against the will of a real ancient or an Antediluvian<br /> My two cent, this probably happened already, just nobody noticed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-05-2022, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T11:00:31-07:00","id":1483157,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I would never assume that any of the sixth generation vampires in the Inner Circle are operating independently of influence from further up their respective family trees.<br /> <br /> If anything, they were selected as a evolution of the Inquisition gambit; a public face to flush out Anarchs and diablerists, but this time with an institutionalized statelike monopoly on violence to put the threats down and maintain order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T11:27:45-07:00","id":1483159,"title":"","content":"I'd say <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Kemintiri#Modern_nights\" target=\"_blank\">Kemintiri</a> - and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Karsh#Speculation\" target=\"_blank\">Karsh</a>, since Revised era - stories make a strong case for that having already happened, more than once even.<br /> <br /> The real question imho is <b>what for</b>. Motivation is key and i suspect most meths &amp; antes have more peculiar interests than herding/micromanaging princes &amp; primogen or playing multi-tiered chess with domains in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T12:42:45-07:00","id":1483163,"title":"","content":"What would happen if a rich and powerful billionaire decided to impose his will over US politics? He\u2019d get in line, that\u2019s what would happen. The political dynamics of the Camarilla are already determined by a complex network of elders, including methuselahs and Antediluvians, pulling the strings behind the scenes. If a new one awoke and starting trying to influence things, they could, but they would still just be one player in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T13:02:21-07:00","id":1483165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483139#post1483139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Inner Circle of the Camarilla has as its members some of the most powerful active vampires. There's a reason the game has kept that more or less secret while giving us the names and even stats of the Justicars. We know that some cities' Princes and Primogen have been extremely powerful and ancient themselves, so the Inner Circle is likely to be at least as old and powerful as people like Khalid, Inyanga, Critias, and Mithras. (Or if not, it's because they are doing the bidding of vampires who are.)<br /> <br /> Any attempt to directly intimidate or force them will meet with huge resistance. Not only by the Inner Circle and their small army of Justicars and Archons, but also some of the Gehenna cults and many other elders. It will put a huge target on their back.<br /> <br /> That's why such ancient and powerful vampires typically choose to act more subtly through pawns or front organizations. Almost assuredly there are Methusalehs and Antedeluvians manipulating the Camarilla as a whole. It's less efficient, but far more safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have inner circle vampires stats and they are weak. Ancillae+ on a good day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T14:38:50-07:00","id":1483175,"title":"","content":"I'm definitely throwing my lot in with the &quot;this is already happening as we speak&quot;. The Methuselahs/Antes simply don't advertise. Why would they?<br /> <br /> The question is not &quot;is the Camarilla controlled by even more ancient and powerful vampires?&quot;. It's &quot;which ones, and to what end?&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T14:59:43-07:00","id":1483178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We have inner circle vampires stats and they are weak. Ancillae+ on a good day. </div> </div> </div>True, their stats are certainly not impressive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They Inner circle would probably politely asked, whats thy bidding my master? </div> </div> </div>This is what I suspect would happen as well. In fact, this is supposed to be one of the things that is implied to have happened according to BJD, in the case of Artemis Orthia telling the Camarilla to destroy every kindred in Tunis (old Carthage) and the Brujah not liking the idea, making them leave the sect, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm definitely throwing my lot in with the &quot;this is already happening as we speak&quot; </div> </div> </div>I feel it's very likely to have already happened on occasion and happening now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why such ancient and powerful vampires typically choose to act more subtly through pawns or front organizations </div> </div> </div>True, most old vampires prefer to act in discreetly, although that's not the case for Artemis and her descendants by the way. They are known to prefer to take power by force and on the open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T15:13:14-07:00","id":1483179,"title":"","content":"In the games I run, you can get a Gen boost by Diablerizing someone of equal or lower Generation, not just one of lower Gen (Gens 1-5 are earned via upgrading your Clan Disciplines). With this in mind, I very much see the Elders of both sects trading their pawns with the intention of Diablerizing them when they get powerful enough. <br /> <br /> So, at least in my games, Methuselahs already are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T00:44:37-07:00","id":1483205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483165#post1483165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have inner circle vampires stats and they are weak. Ancillae+ on a good day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll concede your superior knowledge of canon. But it's unfortunate. Any member of the Inner Circle should be someone capable of speaking on behalf of their clan which implies great personal power and incredible influence (of whatever persuasion) over the other clan elders. If it is someone who is relatively weak for an elder, it should still be someone who is a compromise candidate of the other more powerful elders who blocked each other (and thus theoretically enjoys all their support), or who does the bidding of the real power.<br /> <br /> I wonder if this is a result of characters being revealed in Revised who attempted to tone down some of the more powerful canon NPCs of the earlier eras. (At least Rafael de Corazon had a story that explained why he had such influence among his clan although I wish it was a slightly better one).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T01:16:03-07:00","id":1483206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wonder if this is a result of characters being revealed in Revised who attempted to tone down some of the more powerful canon NPCs of the earlier eras. (At least Rafael de Corazon had a story that explained why he had such influence among his clan although I wish it was a slightly better one). </div> </div> </div>I also guess it does. The fact that they revealed so many character's sheets in Revised and these were mostly terribly made/weak for their position/importance, etc, it did in fact create this impression of weakness. But, to be fair, there were some bad ones in the earlier editions as well, Mithras, given his power and importance (besides his age) didn't have a good character sheet to reflect this and nobody fixed this when they had a chance (e.g. <i>British Isles</i> book), but instead lazily just copied and pasted his old character sheet from the &quot;time before the invention of the wheel&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T13:39:04-07:00","id":1483332,"title":"","content":"In the interest of context, 1st Edition V:tM was this wild time where players were assumed to be Anarchs and Diablerie was assumed to be what Anarchs do. Two of the first published adventures released for the game were Diablerie quests to hunt down sleeping Methusalehs, and offered new Thaumaturgy rituals to make sure an entire coterie got to gain a Generation lift if the Methusaleh they took down together was powerful enough. Important NPC's were statted weak in order to ensure that hunting, killing, and eating them would be a plausible goal. Mithras, to cite one example, was introduced during this period of the game's history.<br /> <br /> I understand and don't necessarily disagree with the argument for strengthening characters who are weaker than an Elder player character who progressed through, say, Transylvania Chronicles would be. There's always going to be a part of me, though, that's tickled by what a cannibalism festival the game once was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 06-07-2022, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T14:36:51-07:00","id":1483336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483332#post1483332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the interest of context, 1st Edition V:tM was this wild time where players were assumed to be Anarchs and Diablerie was assumed to be what Anarchs do. Two of the first published adventures released for the game were Diablerie quests to hunt down sleeping Methusalehs, and offered new Thaumaturgy rituals to make sure an entire coterie got to gain a Generation lift if the Methusaleh they took down together was powerful enough. Important NPC's were statted weak in order to ensure that hunting, killing, and eating them would be a plausible goal. Mithras, to cite one example, was introduced during this period of the game's history.<br /> <br /> I understand and don't necessarily disagree with the argument for strengthening characters who are weaker than an Elder player character who progressed through, say, Transylvania Chronicles would be. There's always going to be a part of me, though, that's tickled by what a cannibalism festival the game once was.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By the way this reminds me of Tiamat, but at least in her case, it was explicitly stated in the text that she was weakened from being freshly awakened and that her traits would be much higher once fully awakened, but the whole theme of the book (Bloody Hearts <b>Diablerie</b> Britain) was indeed what you mentioned, a coterie working with the goal of diablerizing elders and Methuselah, as in this very case, even the name of the book implies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T15:09:20-07:00","id":1483338,"title":"","content":"That's it, and there was another one to take down a fourth- or fifth-generation Gangrel Methusaleh in Mexico.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T15:59:31-07:00","id":1483343,"title":"","content":"Both Diablerie books were written quite early in the game's history (1992 and 1993). Although the game marketed itself as a game of personal horror, White Wolf must have known that many players would be coming into the game from more combat heavy and dungeon exploration games like D&amp;D. I imagined these books were an attempt to appeal to those kinds of players. <br /> <br /> It makes sense. If you look at a lot of early Call of Cthulhu scenarios, they too are combat heavy, monster bashing in dungeon type environments. It took a while before Call of Cthulhu scenarios moved away from the D&amp;D template towards a format more appropriate for Lovecraftian adventures and their rules set. Likewise, I think it took a while for STs and players to learn how a Vampire game is different from other RPGs.<br /> <br /> However, I've always felt that most Vampire adventures/scenarios have generally been quite weak. They are always plot heavy and therefore railroady as opposed to presenting a situation to the PCs and allowing them to react however they want. As such, there were always NPCs who had heavy plot armor, and others made intentionally weak in order to encourage the PCs to take them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T17:38:52-07:00","id":1483349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483338#post1483338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's it, and there was another one to take down a fourth- or fifth-generation Gangrel Methusaleh in Mexico.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This one you mention is that infamous Gangrel who can somehow use Animalism to control Werewolves? I don't remember seeins his character sheet though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T17:41:42-07:00","id":1483350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483343#post1483343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both Diablerie books were written quite early in the game's history (1992 and 1993). Although the game marketed itself as a game of personal horror, White Wolf must have known that many players would be coming into the game from more combat heavy and dungeon exploration games like D&amp;D. I imagined these books were an attempt to appeal to those kinds of players.<br /> <br /> It makes sense. If you look at a lot of early Call of Cthulhu scenarios, they too are combat heavy, monster bashing in dungeon type environments. It took a while before Call of Cthulhu scenarios moved away from the D&amp;D template towards a format more appropriate for Lovecraftian adventures and their rules set. Likewise, I think it took a while for STs and players to learn how a Vampire game is different from other RPGs.<br /> <br /> However, I've always felt that most Vampire adventures/scenarios have generally been quite weak. They are always plot heavy and therefore railroady as opposed to presenting a situation to the PCs and allowing them to react however they want. As such, there were always NPCs who had heavy plot armor, and others made intentionally weak in order to encourage the PCs to take them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, this, I never liked much the idea of &quot;Plot Armor&quot; AKA &quot;Plot Device&quot;, I mean, as I said if I want to make an NPC &quot;all powerful&quot; in order for him to be hard to beat, I make him just that, powerful and very hard to beat, but not <i>impossible </i>to defeat. That's one of the points of making the character sheet for the said NPCs, besides all the others I have cited in earlier posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T22:51:58-07:00","id":1483359,"title":"","content":"I assume they already do control the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T23:37:47-07:00","id":1483361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483359#post1483359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume they already do control the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's sort of the whole point behind the Jihad. Everyone is a puppet, the Camarilla, the Sabbat, the Anarchs, and even those puppetmasters are themselves puppets to others who are playing 6th dimensional chess.<br /> <br /> But ultimately, I think some ancient elder showing up and telling the Camarilla or the Sabbat, &quot;Now I'm in charge&quot; would run into serious issues if she tries to begin changing or modifying any of the basic concepts of the organization because none of those are monolithic top-down organizations. The Prince's and Packs have a fair amount of room to modify or flat out ignore marching orders they're given that they don't agree with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T00:19:32-07:00","id":1483362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483361#post1483361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's sort of the whole point behind the Jihad. Everyone is a puppet, the Camarilla, the Sabbat, the Anarchs, and even those puppetmasters are themselves puppets to others who are playing 6th dimensional chess.<br /> <br /> But ultimately, I think some ancient elder showing up and telling the Camarilla or the Sabbat, &quot;Now I'm in charge&quot; would run into serious issues if she tries to begin changing or modifying any of the basic concepts of the organization because none of those are monolithic top-down organizations. The Prince's and Packs have a fair amount of room to modify or flat out ignore marching orders they're given that they don't agree with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Certainly, it is not like it would be simple for any Methuselah to do it, as there are some powerful Kindred already in charge of the Camarilla, so to speak. But the situation I'm implying here, is one similar to Artemis Orthia in BJD, where she meets the Inner Council and tell them to destroy every Kindred in Tunis or else she's going to force them to. The case is someone of this level of power, someone who is clearly more powerful than anyone in the Inner Council (or perhaps even the Inner Council combined) as it's the case with Orthia or perhaps something less blatant, like the Methuselah saying he wants to be in charge, but doesn't need the Canarilla to change radically, he just wants it to work for his interests, etc.<br /> <br /> So, all in all, this is the very discussion here, what is your usual take on this kind of situation. It's just food for thought, anyway lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T01:51:36-07:00","id":1483363,"title":"","content":"If a Methuselah or an Antediluvian decided to move their plots in the first person, not through puppets and occult influence, and take direct control of part of the Sect they would offer him the armchair without particular problems.<br /> The camarilla is a hierarchy based on seniority, after all, and its very structure takes the oldest vampires to the top.<br /> If they don't do it directly it is because they would draw a big target on themselves in Jyhad, which is why they prefer to subtly influence from the shadows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26315,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26315-querion","user":"Querion","date":". 06-08-2022, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26315-querion","name":"Querion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T06:52:21-07:00","id":1483372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483362#post1483362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Certainly, it is not like it would be simple for any Methuselah to do it, as there are some powerful Kindred already in charge of the Camarilla, so to speak. But the situation I'm implying here, is one similar to Artemis Orthia in BJD, where she meets the Inner Council and tell them to destroy every Kindred in Tunis or else she's going to force them to. The case is someone of this level of power, someone who is clearly more powerful than anyone in the Inner Council (or perhaps even the Inner Council combined) as it's the case with Orthia or perhaps something less blatant, like the Methuselah saying he wants to be in charge, but doesn't need the Canarilla to change radically, he just wants it to work for his interests, etc.<br /> <br /> So, all in all, this is the very discussion here, what is your usual take on this kind of situation. It's just food for thought, anyway lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really I think if any Methuselah showed up in front of the Inner Circle making demands, provided those demands didn't go counter to the Camarilla's goals, the Inner Circle would just add all of that to the queue. It's not really worth getting up in arms over. If the Methuselah was making demands that would endanger the Camarilla, they'd say, &quot;Sure thing boss,&quot; and then do fuck all. <br /> <br /> When that Methuselah showed back up later, he'd find the Inner Council and also several other Methuselahs (the puppet masters) or maybe even <i>those</i> guy's puppet masters (some of whom may have done the exact same thing, showing up in front of the Inner Council several centuries ago demanding to be in charge). And these eldritch methuselahs would make it clear to the newcommer that he can't just muscle in on their turf and the organization they've spent centuries growing, though if he wants to take a seat at the table there's probably an equitable arrangement that can be had that wouldn't risk Final Death for anyone. <br /> <br /> In the end, the Inner Council is basically composed of the vampires who are willing to stick their necks out and be front and center. Behind them are other, older vampires pulling their strings, and older vampires behind them. The whole point of the Jihad is that there's a conspiracy, but even as you unmask one conspiracy you find another one. Sometimes you have a Methuselah. Sometimes you have Baba Yaga. And sometimes you have Vasilisa. Any vampire who is too powerful for the Council to deal with will find himself dealing with other vampires who are as strong, or stronger than them, the ones who are sitting behind the Inner Council. <br /> <br /> Really I would just be very surprised if Artemis Orthia was the first Methuselah to ever do something like this to the Council. It's probably happened several times, and other Methuselah stepped out of the wood work to put the newcomer in their place or give them a seat at the table. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T12:05:01-07:00","id":1483391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Querion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483363#post1483363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Methuselah or an Antediluvian decided to move their plots in the first person, not through puppets and occult influence, and take direct control of part of the Sect they would offer him the armchair without particular problems.<br /> The camarilla is a hierarchy based on seniority, after all, and its very structure takes the oldest vampires to the top.<br /> If they don't do it directly it is because they would draw a big target on themselves in Jyhad, which is why they prefer to subtly influence from the shadows.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure, most Methuselah prefer to act from the shadows, but Artemis Orthia is one of those few that like the idea of doing it personally, in fact it's a trait shared by all her line of descendants. Although one could argue that Mithras isn't much different, as he also likes to let it clear that he's in charge when he acts, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 06-08-2022, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T12:51:20-07:00","id":1483396,"title":"","content":"Perfectly understandable<br /> After all, if you are old and powerful enough to pull such a stunt, you were porbably literally a God to the people, and walked among them, Artemis, Apollo, Mithras, Tiamat, Michael, Odin, Baba Yaga...<br /> On dark nights, the Little Grandmother, the iron-toothed hag, would fly across the skies of Russia on her magic mortar, and under her shadow milk spoiled and babies were born dead, or so they said. When she finally awoke, and the legends were a pale approximation of the truth. She found the world not to her liking, and remade it to her needs, occasionally pausing to swat an arrogant Garou sept out of her way.<br /> Artemis is similar, but paying attention to the lesson given by the destruction of her broodmate Medon, she decided to follow a course of action that so many Ventrue after her would emulate: rather than try to oppose or dominate the growing power of mortal institutions (and risk being overrun in the process), she rode with it, joining the Spartan invigoration to influence the making of history.<br /> As the Lord of Light, Mithras portrayed himself as the bringer of civilization and morality, who spent his days guiding the sun through heavens and thus only appeared at night.<br /> Odin, The All-High ruled the north and was worshiped by some as the one-eyed god Odin and was the center of the Einherjar society. The Einherjar saw themselves as the last of Odin's warriors on Midgard, preparing to fight in the impending Ragnar\u00f6k. The Einherjar rarely have compunction about functioning openly in public. The idea of the Silence of the Blood is a foreign one \u2013 hide from mortal sight? The chosen warriors of Odin? In later days, the Camarilla's Masquerade is seen as a weak and pathetic excuse for power-plays, intrigues among vampires who cannot stand and fight like men.<br /> Realy, when you are ten times older at least than this new fad the youngsters call &quot;Camarilla&quot;, and walked as Gods among the mortals you rarely tolerate the nonsense they hold dear.... <br /> <br /> Kinda refernce:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.riotamot.com/vampire/readArchive.php?IssueNo=201\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.riotamot.com/vampire/readArchive.php?IssueNo=201\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.riotamot.com/vampire/readArchive.php?IssueNo=201\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.riotamot.com/vampire/readArchive.php?IssueNo=201 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T13:34:48-07:00","id":1483400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Odin, The All-High ruled the north and was worshiped by some as the one-eyed god Odin and was the center of the Einherjar society. The Einherjar saw themselves as the last of Odin's warriors on Midgard, preparing to fight in the impending Ragnar\u00f6k. The Einherjar rarely have compunction about functioning openly in public. </div> </div> </div>By the way The All-High is another cainite I wish we had more things published about.<br /> <br /> &quot;What is this Cam-Ah-Rilla you speak of&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Loved the reference <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T22:58:35-07:00","id":1483445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483391#post1483391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, most Methuselah prefer to act from the shadows, but Artemis Orthia is one of those few that like the idea of doing it personally, in fact it's a trait shared by all her line of descendants. Although one could argue that Mithras isn't much different, as he also likes to let it clear that he's in charge when he acts, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Artemis is in fact an exception, and I imagine there are other Cainites of low generation and great age who govern directly, but they can be counted on the fingers of one hand probably.<br /> <br /> Individuals like Baba Yaga or Mitra are a little different. They have ruled or have ruled continuously for millennia, they are known and recognized and have already put in place measures and countermeasures towards their being exposed.<br /> <br /> But here we were talking about a Methuselah who suddenly woke up and took power. I guess it's just plain inexpensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26315-querion","name":"Querion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T08:47:26-07:00","id":1483601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Querion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483445#post1483445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Artemis is in fact an exception, and I imagine there are other Cainites of low generation and great age who govern directly, but they can be counted on the fingers of one hand probably.<br /> <br /> Individuals like Baba Yaga or Mitra are a little different. They have ruled or have ruled continuously for millennia, they are known and recognized and have already put in place measures and countermeasures towards their being exposed.<br /> <br /> But here we were talking about a Methuselah who suddenly woke up and took power. I guess it's just plain inexpensive.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, that's why I didn't count Mithras as being on the same level of &quot;I prefer to do things with my own hands&quot; as Artemis Orthia, but still he holds some similarities, the difference is that he and Baba Yaga were more explored by the setting, while Artemis Orthia suddenly woke up and wondered &quot;What is this Cam-ah-Rilla you speak of?&quot; and then stepped upon the Inner Council making demands to it lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T08:48:53-07:00","id":1483602,"title":"","content":"In any case, Artemis is certainly an exception to the normal rule of &quot;commanding from the shadows&quot; most Methuselah follow...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T08:49:54-07:00","id":1483603,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the Camarilla briefly getting their shit together to deal with the single threat as quickly and efficiently as possible. No way even an Antediluvian would stand a chance against the entire Sect if they closed ranks, thought things through and coordinated their tactics. ...And then going right back to their politicking and double-speak the moment s/he'd fled and gone into torpor.<br /> <br /> A big part of the North-American metaplot in Werewolf: The Forsaken is that an eldritch monster spirit went nuts in the region and a true alliance of tribes brought it down... resulting in a schism between the Uratha who want to mobilize into a more coordinated society to deal with all their problems the same way since it worked so well that one time, and the ones rejecting that mentality as making the packs too interdependent and going against werewolf nature by imitating human systems of centralized authority.<br /> <br /> I feel like the Camerilla could do with a similar event to point to, giving more Cammies reason to strive for earnest solidarity between the clans, and even the Sects, and create some of the same tension. Might sound incompatible with the denial of the existence of Antediluvians, but most kindred with any authority only actually seem to pay lip service to that policy anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27456-mr-sharp","name":"Mr Sharp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T12:22:37-07:00","id":1483633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla#post1483112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what is your take if a powerful Methuselah or Antediluvian awoke and decided to impose his will on the camarilla saying he wants to command the sect, otherwise he's going to force his will or cause havoc in the world?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> you can bet it it would upset the balance of power in the sect and that elders and active ancients would work overtime to to prevent such a being from causing such disruption to there unlives and give groups like the Second Inquistion more knowledge of what they are facing. That is my take on the situation Herr Meister.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T16:48:45-07:00","id":1483660,"title":"","content":"The inner council member are probably are some of the most influential kindred around. A methuselah vs 7 inner council members and the sect they control doesn't even sound fair. Remember what happened to the 2nd gen vampires when younger vampires came for them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T19:46:57-07:00","id":1483679,"title":"","content":"Stupid question, but wasn't the Inner Circle toasted by the Second Inquisition? And aren't the Elders being compelled to the Middle East to have their own &quot;the Gathering?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T19:50:50-07:00","id":1483680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483679#post1483679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stupid question, but wasn't the Inner Circle toasted by the Second Inquisition? And aren't the Elders being compelled to the Middle East to have their own &quot;the Gathering?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The <i>Tremere </i>Inner Council was, allegedly anyway, mostly toasted. As for the Beckoning, it's not all elders just most. Also known as whatever better for the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T10:20:20-07:00","id":1483720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483680#post1483680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The <i>Tremere </i>Inner Council was, allegedly anyway, mostly toasted. As for the Beckoning, it's not all elders just most. Also known as whatever better for the story.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not to mention many elders and ancients have been trying to find ways to stave of the Beckoning like Helen and Mithras seems to be not to compelled to leave England yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T10:28:59-07:00","id":1483722,"title":"","content":"A better question is which anteidulivan would make the effort to impose it's will on the Camarilla at all or any of there eldest direct childer? Would Toreador really bother with the sect if it impedes not enjoying herself in any of the entertainment meccas in the world. Gangrel never seemed to express an interest in the doings of it's clan or sects so that leaves that one out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T12:32:20-07:00","id":1483739,"title":"","content":"The truth is that the WoD is absolutely unrealistic, and Im not talking about it being unrealistic for having magical beings lurking in the shadows, I mean it's unrealistic in the assumptions it makes on how it all works. The only way for any of that to minimally work is if all the demi-gods in it simply dont do nothing for some reason. You just have to pretend that those assumptions work as a background for your game and suspend disbelief in order to play. The minute you begin to SERIOUSLY try to use lvl 8+ disciplines, it all falls apart.<br /> <br /> For the other splats except for Mage, it can still function, but Mage and Vampire is absolutely unrealistic. Having a single mage with 5 level 5 Spheres or a Vampire with lvl 9 in some disciplines like dominate, obfuscate, auspex and a few others is absolutely world breaking, let alone lvl 6 Spheres or 10 disciplines.<br /> <br /> Heck, even Wraith the Oblivion I dont believe it to be possible to maintain. Just a few Renegades possessing some key mortals would already cause havoc in the world, and there are MILLIONS upon millions of Wraiths.<br /> <br /> I did played a table of &quot;Jihad&quot;, were we all played 4th generation guys from the second city. It was the funniest RPG I ever played, but I gotta tell you, we were NOT playing power struggles. We were so powerful that, even thou there were elders stronger than us, not to mention the 3ths, but even then we were so insane that there were really no reason to play the little jihad games of &quot;lesser&quot; vampires. So we just did whatever we wanted while simply respecting other ancient ones of similar or higher state as our own, it we treated each other with some deference and respect, both PCs or NPCs, without any real conflicts. My PC even became a Golconda aspirant, and I retreated from Jihad all togheter. I became a homeless hermit, a sort of a legend, going from city to city and imparting wisdom with total uninterest for any mundane concerns. For example, I &quot;helped&quot; the Brujahs of Carthage - with wisdom and advice, not directly, and I was the tutor of Catherine the Wise. And I told them not to go to war with Rome, but I didnt force them. I never got involved. And I would go to Rome too give advice to the Ventrues there too.<br /> <br /> But really, if I wanted I could destroy both cities so... This is what I mean. It's unrealistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T13:06:50-07:00","id":1483805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483739#post1483739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The truth is that the WoD is absolutely unrealistic, and Im not talking about it being unrealistic for having magical beings lurking in the shadows, I mean it's unrealistic in the assumptions it makes on how it all works. The only way for any of that to minimally work is if all the demi-gods in it simply dont do nothing for some reason. You just have to pretend that those assumptions work as a background for your game and suspend disbelief in order to play. The minute you begin to SERIOUSLY try to use lvl 8+ disciplines, it all falls apart.<br /> <br /> For the other splats except for Mage, it can still function, but Mage and Vampire is absolutely unrealistic. Having a single mage with 5 level 5 Spheres or a Vampire with lvl 9 in some disciplines like dominate, obfuscate, auspex and a few others is absolutely world breaking, let alone lvl 6 Spheres or 10 disciplines.<br /> <br /> Heck, even Wraith the Oblivion I dont believe it to be possible to maintain. Just a few Renegades possessing some key mortals would already cause havoc in the world, and there are MILLIONS upon millions of Wraiths.<br /> <br /> I did played a table of &quot;Jihad&quot;, were we all played 4th generation guys from the second city. It was the funniest RPG I ever played, but I gotta tell you, we were NOT playing power struggles. We were so powerful that, even thou there were elders stronger than us, not to mention the 3ths, but even then we were so insane that there were really no reason to play the little jihad games of &quot;lesser&quot; vampires. So we just did whatever we wanted while simply respecting other ancient ones of similar or higher state as our own, it we treated each other with some deference and respect, both PCs or NPCs, without any real conflicts. My PC even became a Golconda aspirant, and I retreated from Jihad all togheter. I became a homeless hermit, a sort of a legend, going from city to city and imparting wisdom with total uninterest for any mundane concerns. For example, I &quot;helped&quot; the Brujahs of Carthage - with wisdom and advice, not directly, and I was the tutor of Catherine the Wise. And I told them not to go to war with Rome, but I didnt force them. I never got involved. And I would go to Rome too give advice to the Ventrues there too.<br /> <br /> But really, if I wanted I could destroy both cities so... This is what I mean. It's unrealistic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes and no. While yes, some level 8-9 disciplines are kind of &quot;world breaking&quot;, there are also very few stated vampires with this level of power. I know only &quot;half a dozen&quot; Cainites with level 9 power stated, for instance, If I'm not mistaken, only Ur-Shulgi, Goratrix, Elimelech, Michael of Constantinople, Shaitan, Baba Yaga and Mithras have level 9 disciplines in their character's sheet, so this gives a good glimpse of the rarity of such powers. Basically, the thing you said could be said about almost any RPG world (like Forgotten Realms) or Marvel or DC worlds or perhaps even LOTR lol. In all of these worlds there are many demi -gods that could create a lot of havoc around the world if they wanted to, the thing is, I mean, the question is always &quot;what story you want to tell&quot;? Considering the other worlds I cited, I think WoD is most likely the least &quot;unrealistic&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T13:33:22-07:00","id":1483806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killtron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483660#post1483660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inner council member are probably are some of the most influential kindred around. A methuselah vs 7 inner council members and the sect they control doesn't even sound fair. Remember what happened to the 2nd gen vampires when younger vampires came for them</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, if the Inner Circle is the same mentioned in GC, then Shaitan, for instance, would likely kill them all in a single turn lol, or Mithras could dominate them all in a single turn, they don't stand a chance against a powerful Methuselah, they're far from impressive...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T14:18:11-07:00","id":1483812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483806#post1483806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if the Inner Circle is the same mentioned in GC, then Shaitan, for instance, would likely kill them all in a single turn lol, or Mithras could dominate them all in a single turn, they don't stand a chance against a powerful Methuselah, they're far from impressive...</div> </div> </div> </div>Most official sheets are far from impressive in comparison to the lore about the same character, WW always had a tendency to give quite bad stats for the NPCs.<br /> <br /> Add to that that the mechanics of the game not always conform adequately to the lore of the game, otherwise the demise of the Second Generation would also be extremely unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T05:34:57-07:00","id":1483857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most official sheets are far from impressive in comparison to the lore about the same character, WW always had a tendency to give quite bad stats for the NPCs. </div> </div> </div>Finally someone who understands my pain lol, I've always had this impression hahaha<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">otherwise the demise of the Second Generation would also be extremely unlikely.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> But at least in this case, if I'm not mistaken, it was before there was a difference in power between generations, right? So that serves as a &quot;good excuse&quot;.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T08:51:10-07:00","id":1483875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483812#post1483812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the demise of the Second Generation would also be extremely unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny how they suposedly died, yet legends here and there say the second generation actually survived in form or another... Zillah as the Weeping Stone, Irad went to out to the Land of Nod to find Caine when things started to go south (An act, that later was repeted by the suposedly destroyed Ventrue Antediluvian too...) but never returned, and lastly, Enoch as a possibility in the sarcophagus in Beckett's Jyhad Diary...<br /> The Crone deffinitly survived the whole staked and left out on the Sun by Caine thing, since she created the Lihannan later and she was Embraced by Caine too!<br /> Dracian was Embraced by Caine himself during his wanderings and the sire of Ravana and Ennoia and never knew satisfaction and in search of that elusive quality travelled to East, and according to Gypsy lore Dracian has been appointed as the creator of a tree that was the embodiment life and knowledge, full in its age and beauty. It is said that one of the golden fruits of this Tree of Knowledge could cure the eternal thirst for blood in a vampire (as well as bestowing other unknown gifts).<br /> If Azanael was really a 2nd generation vampire who later became a demon like sepcter, posessing a body as per The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra, he is &quot;survived&quot; too...<br /> Really, the only second generation vampires who died and stayed dead are Khe-duk and Liada, the King and Queen of En'esh from the Assamite myth it seems (or rhe Ravnos also say that their progenitor was the &quot;favored childe of Caine&quot;/Kaen and was nailed to the roof of a temple to burn thanks to Ennoia...)<br /> Well them, and the Lovers from the Toreador myths, who are &quot;technically&quot; the first generation and walked out to greet the sun, and by that account the whole second generation thing was a second atempt to create progenies, untill the whole &quot;let each progeny weaker then its sire&quot; curse... wich was a funny and wise move...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T11:09:09-07:00","id":1483888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483857#post1483857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But at least in this case, if I'm not mistaken, it was before there was a difference in power between generations, right? So that serves as a &quot;good excuse&quot;.[/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but that's actually a fairly recent theory. There's no guarantee that this was the case and the books usually seem to assume that there was no such a time and the second and third generations did had a reasonable gap of power between them. What is stated in the Book of Nod IIRC is that the 3rd Generation was the last to have god-like powers, which means less that they had the same level of power and more that those three Generations would see the 4th as Thin Bloods.<br /> <br /> In general the tale of the murder of the 2nd Generation is regarded as a cautionary tale for the dangers of the higher Gen when they get in numbers, and despite the dubious results this theme is repeated during the destruction of Antes in the Dark Ages and even the destruction of Ventrue and Brujah in the Classic times. Those stories don't need to be true to be taken seriously by the characters, so they definitely perceive this as possible. Add to this more low-profile Diableries and political or military victories and the setting is full of lore examples of low gens falling to newer and higher gen vampires.<br /> <br /> This is something the mechanics have a poor time explaining, they simply do not model such outcomes, yet they're clearly meant to be a thing in the setting. This is not a big problem, it is normal that rules have trouble modeling some things. But it does imply that rules shouldn't be taken too literally when analyzing or even defining lore for your game. They're <b>not</b> the characters, they're a <b>representation</b> of the characters, and can fail at that on some aspects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483875#post1483875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny how they suposedly died, yet legends here and there say the second generation actually survived in form or another...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just how legends work.<br /> <br /> Both their survival <b>and</b> their demise are legends. Their very existence is a legend. And with the passing of time it is natural that those legends would appear because this is not about the reality of the facts, but about the stories people make to account for their experiences, perceptions and <i>expectations</i>. The same way we have legends about Elvis surviving, about Jesus surviving, about Caesar surviving.<br /> <br /> You can make those legends be true, or point to some truth in your game. They may be true in the setting and they may be not. But by themselves they're legends and can only be analyzed as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T12:00:54-07:00","id":1483896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483805#post1483805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes and no. While yes, some level 8-9 disciplines are kind of &amp;quot;world breaking&amp;quot;, there are also very few stated vampires with this level of power. I know only &amp;quot;half a dozen&amp;quot; Cainites with level 9 power stated, for instance, If I'm not mistaken, only Ur-Shulgi, Goratrix, Elimelech, Michael of Constantinople, Shaitan, Baba Yaga and Mithras have level 9 disciplines in their character's sheet, so this gives a good glimpse of the rarity of such powers. Basically, the thing you said could be said about almost any RPG world (like Forgotten Realms) or Marvel or DC worlds or perhaps even LOTR lol. In all of these worlds there are many demi -gods that could create a lot of havoc around the world if they wanted to, the thing is, I mean, the question is always &amp;quot;what story you want to tell&amp;quot;? Considering the other worlds I cited, I think WoD is most likely the least &amp;quot;unrealistic&amp;quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Goratrix is a good example. His a relatively young vampire. Why would Goratrix have level 9 disciplines but not Etrius, who have the same power level?<br /> <br /> And what about far older 4th generations? Like Lazarus for instance? And many many others?<br /> <br /> From the top of my head (it has been many years since I played Vampire, so please forgive, many of the names no longer are in my memory), but from what I can remember Kemintiri also had lvl 9 disciplines, and she wasnt even the oldest 4th generation Setite, much less the oldest 4th generation overall. And many many others.<br /> <br /> As for DC and Marvel and D&amp;D worlds, the presence of this beings do cause a MASSIVE impact in the world at large - to the point of sometimes having entire universes &quot;erased&quot; in those stories.<br /> <br /> As for LotR, this is so much true that, in fact, the wars between the Vala against Melkior (the original &quot;Dark Lord&quot; and master of Sauron) did INDEED destroyed the entire world during the First Age, causing the landmasses to crack and Valinor to be physically separated from the Middle Earth - yes, the conflicts of the Gods SANK half of the lands in the world.<br /> <br /> Because of that, the Vala decided to stay away from Middle Earth, and that's why they didnt interfere in the wars of the elves against Morgoth (Melkor), for fear of causing a new global cataclysm (which Eru Illuvatar reprimended them afterwards saying they had little faith, and that Eru would not allow that to happen).<br /> <br /> This is also the reason why the Vala also didnt interfere in the wars against Sauron, especially after the complete destruction of the island nation of Numenor.<br /> <br /> As for Maiar &quot;demi-gods&quot; such as Gandalf or Saruman, their powers were restrained when they went to Middle Earth, so they werent able to that sort of mayhem. The only one capable of that was Sauron himself, but he wanted to rule Middle Earth as a tyrant, not destroy it.<br /> <br /> The Balrog of Moria would be able to something like that, but he (it?) was afraid to leave Moria after the war against the Vala in the end of the first age.<br /> <br /> So, LotR is actually much more balanced in that aspect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T12:35:19-07:00","id":1483898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483888#post1483888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe, but that's actually a fairly recent theory. There's no guarantee that this was the case and the books usually seem to assume that there was no such a time and the second and third generations did had a reasonable gap of power between them. What is stated in the Book of Nod IIRC is that the 3rd Generation was the last to have god-like powers, which means less that they had the same level of power and more that those three Generations would see the 4th as Thin Bloods.<br /> <br /> In general the tale of the murder of the 2nd Generation is regarded as a cautionary tale for the dangers of the higher Gen when they get in numbers, and despite the dubious results this theme is repeated during the destruction of Antes in the Dark Ages and even the destruction of Ventrue and Brujah in the Classic times. Those stories don't need to be true to be taken seriously by the characters, so they definitely perceive this as possible. Add to this more low-profile Diableries and political or military victories and the setting is full of lore examples of low gens falling to newer and higher gen vampires.<br /> <br /> This is something the mechanics have a poor time explaining, they simply do not model such outcomes, yet they're clearly meant to be a thing in the setting. This is not a big problem, it is normal that rules have trouble modeling some things. But it does imply that rules shouldn't be taken too literally when analyzing or even defining lore for your game. They're <b>not</b> the characters, they're a <b>representation</b> of the characters, and can fail at that on some aspects.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's just how legends work.<br /> <br /> Both their survival <b>and</b> their demise are legends. Their very existence is a legend. And with the passing of time it is natural that those legends would appear because this is not about the reality of the facts, but about the stories people make to account for their experiences, perceptions and <i>expectations</i>. The same way we have legends about Elvis surviving, about Jesus surviving, about Caesar surviving.<br /> <br /> You can make those legends be true, or point to some truth in your game. They may be true in the setting and they may be not. But by themselves they're legends and can only be analyzed as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I particularly dont like all those power stories. Yeah, the Ventrue died. Oh no, he was just trolling, he's alive lolololol. Did Ravnos die? Nope! Trololo lolololo<br /> <br /> In truth, I dont like anything above the 5th level. It's just too much for my tastes. And I absolutely like the 3rd generation to be just a legend, let alone the 2nd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T13:02:00-07:00","id":1483902,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what about far older 4th generations? Like Lazarus for instance? And many many others? </div> </div> </div><br /> Kemintiri had a character sheet with level 9 disciplines and Japheth as well, I forgot to mention them. As I wrote, I mentioned stated, I mean characters with traits, Lazarus unfortunately didn't have a character sheet published. The point I made was not that those are the only ones, but more that there are a few with published character's sheet and I forgot to mention Kemintiri and Japheth as it seems. In any case, the point of what I wrote is that these powers are rare, very rare. You'll find maybe one or maybe two active cainites in the whole world with such power. And lol, no, in DC or Marvel worlds you see MANY demi-gods somehow coexisting at the same time and heck you have flash there lol, do you want to compare these worlds' realism with WoD? Also, in reality, there are even few &quot;world breaking&quot; level 9 disciplines at all, Lord of the Rings has much more impressive feats there than what most disciplines from 8-9 level would do. Besides, this is getting utterly and completely out of topic, I mean I don't really care if in your view, there isn't 3rd generation vampires, if your view is contrary to cannon, it's basically the same as if I posted on a thread about the Salubri that the Salubri doesn't exist in my games, even though this is something I took from my head that isn't canon and, perhaps more importantly, is completely off topic...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T14:06:22-07:00","id":1483916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483902#post1483902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Kemintiri had a character sheet with level 9 disciplines and Japheth as well, I forgot to mention them. As I wrote, I mentioned stated, I mean characters with traits, Lazarus unfortunately didn't have a character sheet published. The point I made was not that those are the only ones, but more that there are a few with published character's sheet and I forgot to mention Kemintiri and Japheth as it seems. In any case, the point of what I wrote is that these powers are rare, very rare. You'll find maybe one or maybe two active cainites in the whole world with such power. And lol, no, in DC or Marvel worlds you see MANY demi-gods somehow coexisting at the same time and heck you have flash there lol, do you want to compare these worlds' realism with WoD? Also, in reality, there are even few &quot;world breaking&quot; level 9 disciplines at all, Lord of the Rings has much more impressive feats there than what most disciplines from 8-9 level would do. Besides, this is getting utterly and completely out of topic, I mean I don't really care if in your view, there isn't 3rd generation vampires, if your view is contrary to cannon, it's basically the same as if I posted on a thread about the Salubri that the Salubri doesn't exist in my games, even though this is something I took from my head that isn't canon and, perhaps more importantly, is completely off topic...</div> </div> </div> </div>I was refering to the fact that I dont like bringing those in my games for another subject. Im not saying that they dont exist on cannon. Im merely saying they dont make sense when used. Which is why those powers should be viewed as background - because as you yourself said, Mithras could easily dominate the entire Inner Circle to do his bidding.<br /> <br /> And as Monteparnas clarified, the canon lore dont fit all too well with the Disciplines mechanics, and neither does with the official sheets.<br /> <br /> So, the best we can do is to consider things to be as they are. The Camarilla exists, the Inner Circle exists, and despite of the ever increasing awesomeness of the higher lvl disciplines, the lore doesnt change for having powerful 4ths or 3rds knocking the Inner Circle's door and mass enslaving them. That just doesnt happen, and just because.<br /> <br /> About LotR, there's a reason why all the awesomeness doesnt show, as I've explained. And as for DC and Marvel - particularly DC with Flash as you yourself pointed out, this excessive power leveling is one of the reason why writters are constantly making full reboots of the entire story.<br /> <br /> Edit: it's also why in DC and Marvel you also need a good dose of &quot;suspension of disbelief&quot; to enjoy the stories despite the many clear inconsistencies and impossibilities. I mean, there's absolutely ZERO chance for Batman to be of any help against Darkseid or his minions, except as a &quot;tactical leader&quot; from afar. Yet, we let him join in good faith, because we like Batman and it's kinda cool. But completely nonsensical for him to do it - and yet he does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 06-13-2022, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T14:54:27-07:00","id":1483921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483896#post1483896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because of that, the Vala decided to stay away from Middle Earth, and that's why they didnt interfere in the wars of the elves against Morgoth (Melkor), for fear of causing a new global cataclysm (which Eru Illuvatar reprimended them afterwards saying they had little faith, and that Eru would not allow that to happen).</div> </div> </div> </div>By the way, then they interfered at the end of the war...<br /> <br /> And the whole of Beleriand sank.<br /> <br /> Yet I do think the WoD could be explained in similar ways as to why the grater powers remain in check, as they're by nature also wise enough to know that going too trigger-happy with their greatest powers would cause a reaction from the others and jeopardize their own goals within the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T15:26:54-07:00","id":1483923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About LotR, there's a reason why all the awesomeness doesnt show, </div> </div> </div>Still, as I said, what is shown is already beyond what most level 8-9 disciplines can do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, the best we can do is to consider things to be as they are. The Camarilla exists, the Inner Circle exists, and despite of the ever increasing awesomeness of the higher lvl disciplines, the lore doesnt change for having powerful 4ths or 3rds knocking the Inner Circle's door and mass enslaving them. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I understand, but as I mentioned it's a possibility that a ST could explore at any given time and it's also mentioned in BJD (with the already mentioned case of Artemis Orthia demandind them to kill every cainite in Tunis, basically just because she wants). The main point in the thread was seeing different points of view regarding how these stories would unfold, and most people said the Inner Circle's either already &quot;enslaved&quot;, that is, serving somebody more powerful's interests or they could simply change overnight if a more powerful patron happened to appear before them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it's also why in DC and Marvel you also need a good dose of &quot;suspension of disbelief&quot; to enjoy the stories despite the many clear inconsistencies and impossibilities. I mean, there's absolutely ZERO chance for Batman to be of any help against Darkseid or his minions, except as a &quot;tactical leader&quot; from afar. Yet, we let him join in good faith, because we like Batman and it's kinda cool. But completely nonsensical for him to do it - and yet he does. </div> </div> </div>In this case, I completely agree, because only &quot;suspension of desbelief&quot; can make us (or me at least) enjoy some of the nonsensical things that happen sometimes. In this regard, I think WoD does much better, as there are tons of ways to keep things hidden, so the average player or even 99% of the &quot;NPCs&quot; of the world wouldn't even know if the Inner Circle was dominated (or even exploded in a gigantic blast of fire if the appropriated powers were used to conceal it from &quot;the public view&quot; lol).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yet I do think the WoD could be explained in similar ways as to why the grater powers remain in check, as they're by nature also wise enough to know that going too trigger-happy with their greatest powers would cause a reaction from the others and jeopardize their own goals within the world. </div> </div> </div>One concept I like to use in my games when thinking of powerful NPCs is that power is not limitless, so if one uses something as &quot;world breaking&quot; as the volcanic eruption Menele summoned, the cainite (or the mage, whatever) in question would need some time to &quot;restore his powers&quot;, so to speak. That's one of the reasons I don't like &quot;world breaking&quot; powers having little to no cost, like for instance, systematically, nothing (besides paradox, etc, you get what I mean...) stops a mage from using <i>Ball of Abyssal Flame</i> or <i>Wrath of Apollo</i> &quot;every weekend&quot;, what in my honest opinion should be much more costly in every sense. At least <i>Jaws of the Dracon</i> makes the vampire spend his whole blood reserve and he runs into frenzy after summoning it, something that one might argue is a little costly or dangerous, but in my opinion, not enough or at least not very fitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 06-13-2022, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T07:49:16-07:00","id":1483984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483921#post1483921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, then they interfered at the end of the war...<br /> <br /> And the whole of Beleriand sank.<br /> <br /> Yet I do think the WoD could be explained in similar ways as to why the grater powers remain in check, as they're by nature also wise enough to know that going too trigger-happy with their greatest powers would cause a reaction from the others and jeopardize their own goals within the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's a good explanation that I would totally be behind with (and yes, I forgot that when the Vala finally went to Middle Earth, half of the continent got destroyed lol)<br /> <br /> So indeed, the best explanation here would be, for example: Mithras dont go knocking into the Inner Circle and just &quot;casually&quot; seizing all of the Camarilla because that would trigger an uncountrollable chain reaction of other powers jumping in too with totally unpredictable outcomes.<br /> <br /> And one thing that elder Vampires (or other eldritch powers) do NOT do, is taking unnecessary and uncalculated risks.<br /> <br /> I mean, you dont get to survive for centuries or thousands of years by exposing yourself.<br /> <br /> One thing that I have always been clear in my mind is that, powerful beings are OLD - for the simple reason that it takes a looooong time to master all the &quot;magic&quot; powers of the many kinds of critters in the WoD.<br /> <br /> So, the older you are, the more powerful you'll be.<br /> <br /> There's one problem thou: you dont get to become old enough to become powerful enough to not worry about treats if during the course of time needed to reach that power level if you just kept risking your neck all the time.<br /> <br /> Taking risks works for &quot;newbies&quot; in the WoD. It's how neonate vamps can get favors from elders, it's how apprentice mages can secure a Node or gain favors from masters, or how Werebeasts gain honor and fetishes, or how young Wraiths can secure a few initial promotions.<br /> <br /> That's, however, also how you get yourself killed.<br /> <br /> So, the older a critter is, the more averse it will have to be to take risks - even thou it has more power to bear.<br /> <br /> Or, at the very least, &quot;natural selection&quot; will make sure that &quot;bravery&quot; is rewarded with a &quot;premature&quot; death.<br /> <br /> So, vamps and wraiths and mages with centuries or millenia of baggage will have the tendency of being COWARDS. And paranoid.<br /> <br /> So in my view that's what keeps those powers in check. They are so hesitant to stick their necks above the sand and risk their several life-times of hard work to reach the place they are now, that they just hide, cowering in fear of the slightest treat to their existance.<br /> <br /> The most they do is to keep tabs on the &quot;lessers&quot;, trying to set pawns in motion to crush ANY possibility that SOMEDAY someone COULD become a threat to them.<br /> <br /> There is, they make cold calculations: how risky is it for me to get out of my lair in order to turn X critter into my personal pawn? Is it worth it? Can this pawn be used to crush A, B and C threats to myself? What would be more risky, to enlist my X pawn or to let threats A, B and C proliferate?<br /> <br /> If the answer is that acting to try to prevent a possible threat is MORE risky than not acting, than they simply DONT DO ANYTHING.<br /> <br /> That's how I would envision the mindset of elders to be due to pure natural selection - and the eldest you are, the most pronounced this would be.<br /> <br /> This would lead to a world that is ruled by ancillas and not so old elders, with some freedom for neonates under the eyesight of those &quot;new elders&quot; and only very small and pontual interferences from the true Methuselas that would be imperceptible to most of the young blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T08:23:06-07:00","id":1483986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483923#post1483923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I understand, but as I mentioned it's a possibility that a ST could explore at any given time and it's also mentioned in BJD (with the already mentioned case of Artemis Orthia demandind them to kill every cainite in Tunis, basically just because she wants). The main point in the thread was seeing different points of view regarding how these stories would unfold, and most people said the Inner Circle's either already &amp;quot;enslaved&amp;quot;, that is, serving somebody more powerful's interests or they could simply change overnight if a more powerful patron happened to appear before them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well. So, what could happen in this case is an &quot;elders army race&quot;, upon which several Methusas and Antis get out of their lairs to deal with this issue, because the threat level now has reached unsustainable levels - just check my previous post above this one about how the old powers of WoD behave in relation to perceived threats.<br /> <br /> The challenge of a Methusa going out in the open is a threat TOO BIG to be ignored by ANYONE of similar or higher stature, and would FORCE a bunch of dinossaurs to leave the relative safety of their lairs and to take a more hands on approach.<br /> <br /> This... Would end badly. Bravery is more like foolishness if your plan is to live for some thousands of years. If you managed to be a coward for 1.000 years, deciding to be brave after all that time is... Stupid. All the other cowards which were also hidding for 1000+ years would be forced to act against you... And they would probably try to have some extra punch in order to make sure that you are utterly destroyed and wont try to pull a similar stunt ever again.<br /> <br /> This could include Methusas and Antis temporarily joining forces into uneasy alliances, while they seek to mind control / dominate Anarchists, Sabbat, independent clans, while yet other Methusas go on trying to break the Camarilla apart, dominating one elder here, another there, poisoning those against the Camarilla, starting more anarchist rebellions, etc etc etc.<br /> <br /> Be that as it may, this would probably cause a MASSIVE reaction with ripples throghout the entire Kindred society, as the other Methusas and Antis try to eject the undesired element as anti-body cells attack a disease.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483923#post1483923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One concept I like to use in my games when thinking of powerful NPCs is that power is not limitless, so if one uses something as &amp;quot;world breaking&amp;quot; as the volcanic eruption Menele summoned, the cainite (or the mage, whatever) in question would need some time to &amp;quot;restore his powers&amp;quot;, so to speak. That's one of the reasons I don't like &amp;quot;world breaking&amp;quot; powers having little to no cost, like for instance, systematically, nothing (besides paradox, etc, you get what I mean...) stops a mage from using <i>Ball of Abyssal Flame</i> or <i>Wrath of Apollo</i> &amp;quot;every weekend&amp;quot;, what in my honest opinion should be much more costly in every sense. At least <i>Jaws of the Dracon</i> makes the vampire spend his whole blood reserve and he runs into frenzy after summoning it, something that one might argue is a little costly or dangerous, but in my opinion, not enough or at least not very fitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is one way to deal with it. The other is to say simply that the &quot;Ball of Abyssal Flame&quot; or the &quot;Wrath of Apollo&quot;, or even the &quot;Planetary Gateway to the Thousand Hells&quot; are like using nukes. It's MAD doctrine - Mutually Assured Destruction. If your Mage summons the &quot;City Obliterator&quot;, another Arch-Mage / Oracle / Master Technocrat will unleash the &quot;Planetary Breaker Death-Ray&quot; on your skin.<br /> <br /> That's one of the things from Mage 3e (revised), with the Avatar Storm. The Technocrats decided to go crazy and unleash fanthom destruction to end those &quot;pesky traditions&quot;, and the result was the death of most archies/masters on both sides and ripple effects that basically broke the spiritual world.<br /> <br /> Of course, the problem of this approach is that one side may be crazy enough not to care... Marauders for example. Or Nefandi. A Nefandi master may decide to hide for a few centuries to gather enough power, and one day simply decide to make a show in an expectacular display of destructive abandom. Or a Baali vampire could do that too.<br /> <br /> So, there's always pros and cons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T09:49:41-07:00","id":1483998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1483986#post1483986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is one way to deal with it. The other is to say simply that the &quot;Ball of Abyssal Flame&quot; or the &quot;Wrath of Apollo&quot;, or even the &quot;Planetary Gateway to the Thousand Hells&quot; are like using nukes. It's MAD doctrine - Mutually Assured Destruction. If your Mage summons the &quot;City Obliterator&quot;, another Arch-Mage / Oracle / Master Technocrat will unleash the &quot;Planetary Breaker Death-Ray&quot; on your skin.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take is similar to this, with the added concern for collateral damage breaking your actual plans.<br /> <br /> A Mage don't use a Nuke option just because they can. They use it when they think the benefits outweigh the costs. And the cost isn't just Quintessence or time doing a ritual. The cost is every undesirable consequence that will come from the Nuke.<br /> <br /> Reputation is a very effective cost. If you use a Nuclear Option for giggles, you'll be known by that by enemies and friends alike. Maybe you'll end up without any friends, as happened to Czar Vargo: he tried to conquer the world directly, all other Mages united, kicked his sorry ass and erased him from the <i>fucking time-stream</i>. Even in a lesser situation, people will be at the very least wary of association with someone that goes nuclear without concern for collateral damage, and enemies will be understandably more aggressive.<br /> <br /> Losing your actual goals is also a strong possibility. Not only can you end up breaking the things you actually want, you also encourage others to go for your vulnerable assets and loved ones with more gusto. If you don't hold your horses, they shouldn't either. No one needs to be as strong as you to mess with your family, friends, collections, country club, and your ability to avenge your things won't change their untimely obliteration.<br /> <br /> Using a Nuclear Option without care invites Nuclear consequences on your head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T11:20:50-07:00","id":1484009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, the problem of this approach is that one side may be crazy enough not to care... Marauders for example. Or Nefandi. A Nefandi master may decide to hide for a few centuries to gather enough power, and one day simply decide to make a show in an expectacular display of destructive abandom. Or a Baali vampire could do that too. </div> </div> </div>This is exactly the reason why I prefer to make such things costly. Of course there's also the natural consequence of creating a chain reaction, so to speak, but still I've always felt that many highly destructive powers are rather way too cheap in WoD. I always have to think about &quot;which reason besides narrative could explain why this all-powerful NPC isn't going to simply destroy the PCs from afar?&quot; and I think adding in costs is also interesting. I like the idea of characters who &quot;spent&quot; a great deal of their powers through the ages and, as a consequence, are not as powerful as they used to be. It kind of reminds me of LOTR or Silmarillion, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T12:20:51-07:00","id":1484025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484009#post1484009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is exactly the reason why I prefer to make such things costly. Of course there's also the natural consequence of creating a chain reaction, so to speak, but still I've always felt that many highly destructive powers are rather way too cheap in WoD. I always have to think about &amp;quot;which reason besides narrative could explain why this all-powerful NPC isn't going to simply destroy the PCs from afar?&amp;quot; and I think adding in costs is also interesting. I like the idea of characters who &amp;quot;spent&amp;quot; a great deal of their powers through the ages and, as a consequence, are not as powerful as they used to be. It kind of reminds me of LOTR or Silmarillion, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im a player of Gurps, and in Gurps you can actually spend character points to buy successes or &quot;serendipituous&quot; occurances. I use this in my Gurps games to explain why the Fae get weaker by the ages - they literally spend themselves using their magic, up to the point of their undoing.<br /> <br /> For D10 it aint as easy in the game mechanics, but it can still be part of the lore","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T15:18:31-07:00","id":1484048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For D10 it aint as easy in the game mechanics, but it can still be part of the lore </div> </div> </div>I don't think the cost needs to be so high as to demand the spending of a <i>permanent</i> point of a trait, but at the very least it's a good idea to limit the frequency that &quot;all-powerful&quot; beings use their most destructive powers. It avoids situations like a mighty koldun destroying an entire town with the fury of the elements and waking up the next day as if nothing happened and ready to strike again, for instance lol<br /> <br /> Although now, after writing that,, to be honest, I think it might be a good idea to give a <i>permanent</i> cost to things like Hermetic's <i>Ball of Abyssal Flame</i> or Koldun's <i>Jaws of the Dracon</i>, as I think such powers should never be used &quot;lightly&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T18:30:56-07:00","id":1484080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484048#post1484048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the cost needs to be so high as to demand the spending of a <i>permanent</i> point of a trait, but at the very least it's a good idea to limit the frequency that &quot;all-powerful&quot; beings use their most destructive powers. It avoids situations like a mighty koldun destroying an entire town with the fury of the elements and waking up the next day as if nothing happened and ready to strike again, for instance lol</div> </div> </div> </div>You may consider preparation instead of cost, making the process of enact such a power complex and time and resource-consuming.<br /> <br /> For example, it may demand a Koldun to craft four idols from the earth of the area to be affected, drench them on your blood for a full moon and put then on each cardinal vertex of the area. Now you have a power with a cost that can't be taken lightly or enacted on the fly, without the need for too steep costs on the character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T18:37:43-07:00","id":1484081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484080#post1484080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may consider preparation instead of cost, making the process of enact such a power complex and time and resource-consuming.<br /> <br /> For example, it may demand a Koldun to craft four idols from the earth of the area to be affected, drench them on your blood for a full moon and put then on each cardinal vertex of the area. Now you have a power with a cost that can't be taken lightly or enacted on the fly, without the need for too steep costs on the character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds really cool! I sometimes wish every &quot;high level power&quot; had Willpower in its costs, as that is usually means the character is somehow &quot;spent&quot; after doing something that requires his utter concentration and power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T04:03:55-07:00","id":1484100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484048#post1484048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think the cost needs to be so high as to demand the spending of a <i>permanent</i> point of a trait, but at the very least it's a good idea to limit the frequency that &amp;quot;all-powerful&amp;quot; beings use their most destructive powers. It avoids situations like a mighty koldun destroying an entire town with the fury of the elements and waking up the next day as if nothing happened and ready to strike again, for instance lol<br /> <br /> Although now, after writing that,, to be honest, I think it might be a good idea to give a <i>permanent</i> cost to things like Hermetic's <i>Ball of Abyssal Flame</i> or Koldun's <i>Jaws of the Dracon</i>, as I think such powers should never be used &amp;quot;lightly&amp;quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Gurps is entirely built on character points; most &quot;common adventurers&quot; begin with 200 points, but monsters, super-humans and supernatural beings can be built with a lot more. The True Fae of old could have 2000 or more points.<br /> <br /> There are OPTIONAL rules for spending Char Points to &quot;buy success&quot; - 2 points change critical failure to normal failure, 1 pt to failure to 0 margin success and 2 pts to success for critical success. So, 5 pts change critical failure to critical success.<br /> <br /> On top of that, you can use char points to buy &quot;serendipituous coincidences&quot;; for example, with 1 point you could say &quot;I hide behind the desk&quot;, if the ST didnt say anything about a desk in the room before; while a BELIEVABLE but INCREDIBLE coincidence would cost 3 points - like saying &quot;I open the desk's door to grab the hidden gun inside&quot;.<br /> <br /> It can also be used for &quot;one use only&quot; powers. So, while my Fae do have permanent &quot;Cantrips&quot; and other powers, sometimes they want a little bit more &quot;mojo&quot;. And that's when they spend themselves.<br /> <br /> It can be done on similar grounds for D10 too. Char Points can be sacrificed from spent points, or reducing traits to &quot;un-buy&quot; the points. For example, Attribute costs &quot;Current lvl x 4&quot;. So, if you have for example Strenght 4, from 3 to 4 it costs 12 points, so you could &quot;spend yourself&quot;, reducing your Strenght from 4 to 3 and liberating 12 char points to spend on your wicked plans.<br /> <br /> I really like this - not for players who are power-hungry maniacs of course, but I like the idea of this concept, self destructive beings capable of wielding great powers - for a while. And while they exist, they burn like a bright star, up to the point of consuming themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T12:45:13-07:00","id":1484128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484081#post1484081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds really cool! I sometimes wish every &quot;high level power&quot; had Willpower in its costs, as that is usually means the character is somehow &quot;spent&quot; after doing something that requires his utter concentration and power.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you like the concept I presented, I think the best WoD mechanic to adapt for it would be Changeling <b><i>Bunks</i></b>. You can adapt the bonus to Difficulty into something else, like Power Level, so, lets say, a -1 becomes instead the requisite &quot;Bunk&quot; for levels 1 and 2 powers, while a -5 is instead the requisite for levels 9 and 10.<br /> <br /> Personally I find Changeling's guidelines for Bunks simple to understand and implement and exceedingly useful for the purpose of letting ritual performance be simultaneously versatile and balanced for the game, better than similar guidelines in Mage while avoiding making too strict and numerous descriptions for each power in the way Blood Magic rituals currently work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484100#post1484100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like this - not for players who are power-hungry maniacs of course, but I like the idea of this concept, self destructive beings capable of wielding great powers - for a while. And while they exist, they burn like a bright star, up to the point of consuming themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I think M&amp;M 2nd Edition + Ultimate Power does GURPS' work better and in a simpler way. I've played and GM'd GURPS too and while versatile, and its core rules are simple, really using it to its full power is excessively complex and rigid. M&amp;M achieves mostly the same goals with far simpler and more elegant base rules, far easier to apply. Not 3rd edition, though, its Base Ability system is a load of crap that undoes most of the versatility 2nd edition had. <br /> <br /> An it has this same option built in, but in more ways, as you have Action Points to achieve the same if you don't want to burn Character Points, yet you can apply the same &quot;self-burning&quot; theme in lots of ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T16:31:29-07:00","id":1484147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It can be done on similar grounds for D10 too. Char Points can be sacrificed from spent points, or reducing traits to &quot;un-buy&quot; the points. For example, Attribute costs &quot;Current lvl x 4&quot;. So, if you have for example Strenght 4, from 3 to 4 it costs 12 points, so you could &quot;spend yourself&quot;, reducing your Strenght from 4 to 3 and liberating 12 char points to spend on your wicked plans. </div> </div> </div>I have to say that I qite like the idea, but as you mentioned, players are probably not going to like it. In any case, I can use it for my most powerful NPCs when they perform &quot;mythological feats of power&quot;. Just need to figure out a way to adapt it systematically, so to speak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you like the concept I presented, I think the best WoD mechanic to adapt for it would be Changeling <b><i>Bunks</i></b>. You can adapt the bonus to Difficulty into something else, like Power Level, so, lets say, a -1 becomes instead the requisite &quot;Bunk&quot; for levels 1 and 2 powers, while a -5 is instead the requisite for levels 9 and 10. </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of bunks too, just feel that unfortunately they're often very focused on the modern setting (e.g. &quot;Skydiving without a parachute&quot;), as if I remember correctly, there isn't a similar thing in Dark Ages Fae, although it's been a long time since I read that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T17:13:31-07:00","id":1484152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484147#post1484147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of bunks too, just feel that unfortunately they're often very focused on the modern setting (e.g. &quot;Skydiving without a parachute&quot;), as if I remember correctly, there isn't a similar thing in Dark Ages Fae, although it's been a long time since I read that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The general guidelines are more important than the examples. Break it into a set of quick questions and use them to determine the value of the Bunk:<ul><li><b>How much risk?</b> If performing the Bunk itself carries significant risk, like serious injury, it is a little stronger. If it has significant death risk, it is a lot stronger;<br /> \u200b</li> <li><b>How much Time Consuming?</b> Requiring a lot of time to perform before completion is a little stronger, and increases if it requires the setup of a demanding routine like repeating procedures every day for days at the same hour;<br /> \u200b</li> <li><b>How much investment?</b> If the character has to dedicate a meaningful amount of personal resources or relevant belongings, it is stronger. I'd say something that makes a benefit temporarily unavailable or reduced is a little better, if the loss is permanent it is a lot stronger;<br /> \u200b</li> <li><b>How much is it dramatically appropriate?</b> That's a good one because you can read it however you want to set the theme and mood of the game. If it strongly reinforces them in the context of the scene and pleases you, it is as stronger as you deems fit;<br /> \u200b</li> <li><b>How much does it makes the game enjoyable?</b> Same as above, but for other players. If everyone's clearly enjoying the scene and the description of the Bunk, making it work is probably a good idea.</li> <li><b>How much does it counts for real?</b> If anything here will just fill downtime description instead of actually impacting the game, you can and should freely reduce or outright ignore any benefit of that aspect, at your discretion. Either because it is chaotic, depends on Meaning, or is so rigidly complex that each time little nuances alter the outcome, &quot;magic&quot; of any sort isn't uniform.</li> </ul><br /> Get that and think of the &quot;littles&quot; and &quot;lots&quot; as dials: their precise effects depend on what you want to take out of it and shape the scene accordingly. If you want a rule of thumb, just making a &quot;bunk&quot; is a &quot;Rank 1&quot;, each &quot;little&quot; is a +1 and each &quot;lot&quot; is a +2, then check each of the first three questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T19:01:27-07:00","id":1484160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484152#post1484152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general guidelines are more important than the examples. Break it into a set of quick questions and use them to determine the value of the Bunk:<ul><li><b>How much risk?</b> If performing the Bunk itself carries significant risk, like serious injury, it is a little stronger. If it has significant death risk, it is a lot stronger;<br /> \u200b</li> <li><b>How much Time Consuming?</b> Requiring a lot of time to perform before completion is a little stronger, and increases if it requires the setup of a demanding routine like repeating procedures every day for days at the same hour;<br /> \u200b</li> <li><b>How much investment?</b> If the character has to dedicate a meaningful amount of personal resources or relevant belongings, it is stronger. I'd say something that makes a benefit temporarily unavailable or reduced is a little better, if the loss is permanent it is a lot stronger;<br /> \u200b</li> <li><b>How much is it dramatically appropriate?</b> That's a good one because you can read it however you want to set the theme and mood of the game. If it strongly reinforces them in the context of the scene and pleases you, it is as stronger as you deems fit;<br /> \u200b</li> <li><b>How much does it makes the game enjoyable?</b> Same as above, but for other players. If everyone's clearly enjoying the scene and the description of the Bunk, making it work is probably a good idea.</li> <li><b>How much does it counts for real?</b> If anything here will just fill downtime description instead of actually impacting the game, you can and should freely reduce or outright ignore any benefit of that aspect, at your discretion. Either because it is chaotic, depends on Meaning, or is so rigidly complex that each time little nuances alter the outcome, &quot;magic&quot; of any sort isn't uniform.</li> </ul>Get that and think of the &quot;littles&quot; and &quot;lots&quot; as dials: their precise effects depend on what you want to take out of it and shape the scene accordingly. If you want a rule of thumb, just making a &quot;bunk&quot; is a &quot;Rank 1&quot;, each &quot;little&quot; is a +1 and each &quot;lot&quot; is a +2, then check each of the first three questions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, these guidelines are indeed very interesting, probably even more so than the ones usually provided in Mage books. In any case, these are things we should actually always keep in mind, still I'd think I would prefer the idea of consuming one's own power or as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24689\" data-vbnamecard=\"24689\">Kakost</a> beautifully put it, &quot;burn like bright starts, consuming themselves&quot;.<br /> <br /> Another thing I think is that we lack any &quot;personified power&quot; on the same level of a Mithras, Goratrix, Artemis Orthia, Helena or Menele in the Inner Council and it makes it hard to believe they could really enforce their authority over cainites of this caliber. Even Karsh obeying the Inner Council is only believably if you adopt the thought that the true Hardestadt is still around and not &quot;the younger&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 06-15-2022, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T19:31:14-07:00","id":1484163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484128#post1484128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I think M&amp;M 2nd Edition + Ultimate Power does GURPS' work better and in a simpler way. I've played and GM'd GURPS too and while versatile, and its core rules are simple, really using it to its full power is excessively complex and rigid. M&amp;M achieves mostly the same goals with far simpler and more elegant base rules, far easier to apply. Not 3rd edition, though, its Base Ability system is a load of crap that undoes most of the versatility 2nd edition had. <br /> <br /> An it has this same option built in, but in more ways, as you have Action Points to achieve the same if you don't want to burn Character Points, yet you can apply the same &amp;quot;self-burning&amp;quot; theme in lots of ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont know what this M&amp;M is, althought it sure seems interesring. For Gurps there are rules for &quot;player guidance&quot; that allows using char points, but there are also rules that allow do that without spending permanent points, or rather &quot;spending&quot; a pool of points, but those are renewable (so you dont really spend yourself).<br /> <br /> Those are all optional rules anyway, I just mentioned it because it's interesting for a few concepts. Obviously players will NEVER spend their precious points, but it can still serve for NPCs, at least conceptually, to go down in a &quot;blaze of glory&quot;.<br /> <br /> What is this M&amp;M you were talking about? I'll give it a look","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T19:58:36-07:00","id":1484166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484160#post1484160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, these guidelines are indeed very interesting, probably even more so than the ones usually provided in Mage books. In any case, these are things we should actually always keep in mind, still I'd think I would prefer the idea of consuming one's own power or as <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> beautifully put it, &amp;quot;burn like bright starts, consuming themselves&amp;quot;. <br /> <br /> Another thing I think is that we lack any &amp;quot;personified power&amp;quot; on the same level of a Mithras or Helena and Menele in the Inner Council and it makes it hard to believe they could really enforce their authority over cainites of this caliber.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a few suggestions I could give in THAT specific sense, could be:<br /> <br /> - First: once you start spending yourself, it's a one way road. You can reduce ANY trait at will in order to collect the XP to &quot;fuel&quot; your powers - but you will NEVER be able to use XP EVER again to grow that trait.<br /> * From this, anyone that decides to go this route have 2 options: either keep consuming that single trait, because it will never grow back again, all the way up to the max possible (so, all the way up to reduce it to zero in case of Skills, Disciplines, Spheres, Arcanoi etc, or at most 1 for attributes), but still being able to improve all other traits, or reduce just a little from several traits, maybe just a single dot, but in that case becoming &quot;locked&quot; on several traits.<br /> <br /> The other thing to notice is how will this have diminishing returns - if you reduce strenght from 5 to 4, that frees 16 XP (from 4 to 5 is 4x4). But, from 4 to 3 it's only gonna be 12 XP.<br /> This means that, the more you spend yourself, the more of your own you'd have to burn to achieve the same results. That way, you'd truly burn like a bright star, consuming your own life force with more and more intensity.<br /> <br /> Now, ideas on how to use it:<br /> - Automatic successes, that's an obvious one. Each 1 XP buys 1 success.<br /> <br /> But it needs not be just that. It can also be:<br /> - One use powers: could you REALLY use some Life 4 or 5, but your Life is only 2, or you dont even have it? NO PROBLEM! Just buy it for this one time only... For a price... Could you really use that Dominate 6 but you dont even have the discipline? That's okay!<br /> <br /> Now, this is just a matter of fine tuning the costs, this would actually require some tests, but perhaps 1 XP per necessary traits could be a good initial value. That includes secondary traits required for the use of that power. For example: if you're a gen 11 vamp and you want to make a 1 use of Dominate 6 without any dot in the Discipline, you would first need to be gen 7 - there is, you would need 4 reductions in your generation. Summed up with the 6 dots on Dominate, that would give a total of 10 XP required for a 11 gen vamp with no dots on Dominate to use it for a single time at lvl 6. After using it one time, those points are gone.<br /> <br /> With rules like this, you could have for example some crazy monster hunters blessed by the heavens, but who can only fight for as long as their &quot;celestial mojo&quot; is there.<br /> <br /> If you know the character Spawn from comics, he initially was like that too, Spawn had a limited amount of Ectoplasmic energy, which he could use to be basically a demi-god... However, if he ever went out of &quot;juicy&quot;, he would die. At least at the beggining, before he ended up defeating the Devil Malebolgia and... a ton of other stuff happened.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it is an interesting concept for some cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T20:33:48-07:00","id":1484171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484163#post1484163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is this M&amp;M you were talking about? I'll give it a look</div> </div> </div> </div>Is a game called <i><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/19910/Mutants--Masterminds-Second-Edition\" target=\"_blank\">Mutants &amp; Masterminds 2nd Edition</a></i>, plus its supplement <i><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/20696/Ultimate-Power?src=also_purchased\" target=\"_blank\">Ultimate Power</a></i>. It has many others, but with core plus UP you basically have the full tool-set, anything else will just give youtips and suggestions on how to use it and examples of builds with this tool-set.<br /> <br /> The game was obviously born as a Supers game, but by necessity it tried to be as versatile a toolbox as possible for powers. The 2nd Edition came at the time of the OGL d20 boom of the 2000's, and freeing the developers from building the basic system gave them a lot of time and space in the book to build on other aspects of the game.<br /> <br /> Finally, this specific supplement came as a kind of <i>Unearthed Arcana</i> for the edition, deeply exploring the mechanics of character creation and how to tweak them, and applying several concepts took from computer logic to expand possibilities. The end result is ime the most perfect balance between a robust, comprehensive and broadly applicable RPG system to design any character and simplicity to have all its power available without need for either too many books or many complex calculations.<br /> <br /> Again, I know GURPS have both simplicity and versatility, but not quite at the same time. M&amp;M will also get more complex as you dive in, but it will have a <b>far</b> better pay-off in the versatility:complexity ratio, and with less books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T04:10:22-07:00","id":1484197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484166#post1484166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, a few suggestions I could give in THAT specific sense, could be:<br /> <br /> - First: once you start spending yourself, it's a one way road. You can reduce ANY trait at will in order to collect the XP to &quot;fuel&quot; your powers - but you will NEVER be able to use XP EVER again to grow that trait.<br /> * From this, anyone that decides to go this route have 2 options: either keep consuming that single trait, because it will never grow back again, all the way up to the max possible (so, all the way up to reduce it to zero in case of Skills, Disciplines, Spheres, Arcanoi etc, or at most 1 for attributes), but still being able to improve all other traits, or reduce just a little from several traits, maybe just a single dot, but in that case becoming &quot;locked&quot; on several traits.<br /> <br /> The other thing to notice is how will this have diminishing returns - if you reduce strenght from 5 to 4, that frees 16 XP (from 4 to 5 is 4x4). But, from 4 to 3 it's only gonna be 12 XP.<br /> This means that, the more you spend yourself, the more of your own you'd have to burn to achieve the same results. That way, you'd truly burn like a bright star, consuming your own life force with more and more intensity.<br /> <br /> Now, ideas on how to use it:<br /> - Automatic successes, that's an obvious one. Each 1 XP buys 1 success.<br /> <br /> But it needs not be just that. It can also be:<br /> - One use powers: could you REALLY use some Life 4 or 5, but your Life is only 2, or you dont even have it? NO PROBLEM! Just buy it for this one time only... For a price... Could you really use that Dominate 6 but you dont even have the discipline? That's okay!<br /> <br /> Now, this is just a matter of fine tuning the costs, this would actually require some tests, but perhaps 1 XP per necessary traits could be a good initial value. That includes secondary traits required for the use of that power. For example: if you're a gen 11 vamp and you want to make a 1 use of Dominate 6 without any dot in the Discipline, you would first need to be gen 7 - there is, you would need 4 reductions in your generation. Summed up with the 6 dots on Dominate, that would give a total of 10 XP required for a 11 gen vamp with no dots on Dominate to use it for a single time at lvl 6. After using it one time, those points are gone.<br /> <br /> With rules like this, you could have for example some crazy monster hunters blessed by the heavens, but who can only fight for as long as their &quot;celestial mojo&quot; is there.<br /> <br /> If you know the character Spawn from comics, he initially was like that too, Spawn had a limited amount of Ectoplasmic energy, which he could use to be basically a demi-god... However, if he ever went out of &quot;juicy&quot;, he would die. At least at the beggining, before he ended up defeating the Devil Malebolgia and... a ton of other stuff happened.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it is an interesting concept for some cases.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds interesting, although I want to use it sparingly, just when really powerful characters evoke some very &quot;awesome power&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T06:11:35-07:00","id":1484205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484171#post1484171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is a game called <i><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/19910/Mutants--Masterminds-Second-Edition&amp;quot;]Mutants</a> &amp; Masterminds 2nd Edition[/URL]</i>, plus its supplement <i><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/20696/Ultimate-Power?src=also_purchased&amp;quot;]Ultimate</a> Power[/URL]</i>. It has many others, but with core plus UP you basically have the full tool-set, anything else will just give youtips and suggestions on how to use it and examples of builds with this tool-set.<br /> <br /> The game was obviously born as a Supers game, but by necessity it tried to be as versatile a toolbox as possible for powers. The 2nd Edition came at the time of the OGL d20 boom of the 2000's, and freeing the developers from building the basic system gave them a lot of time and space in the book to build on other aspects of the game.<br /> <br /> Finally, this specific supplement came as a kind of <i>Unearthed Arcana</i> for the edition, deeply exploring the mechanics of character creation and how to tweak them, and applying several concepts took from computer logic to expand possibilities. The end result is ime the most perfect balance between a robust, comprehensive and broadly applicable RPG system to design any character and simplicity to have all its power available without need for either too many books or many complex calculations.<br /> <br /> Again, I know GURPS have both simplicity and versatility, but not quite at the same time. M&amp;M will also get more complex as you dive in, but it will have a <b>far</b> better pay-off in the versatility:complexity ratio, and with less books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see thanks a lot, I'll give it a try","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T09:49:26-07:00","id":1484367,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Kakost;n1483896]<br /> <br /> Goratrix is a good example. His a relatively young vampire. Why would Goratrix have level 9 disciplines but not Etrius, who have the same power level?<br /> <br /> That does not bother me at all. Are we are equally athletic, charming, knowledgeable in all fields? No we are not and maybe charcters of the same generation and different ages would have their own strengths &amp; weaknesses<br /> <br /> And what about far older 4th generations? Like Lazarus for instance? And many many others?<br /> <br /> Lazarus much like Dracon, Montano, Cybil, and many others were not stated. Though we can safely assume that they have max dots in at least two or three disciplines, attributes and skills. <br /> <br /> From the top of my head (it has been many years since I played Vampire, so please forgive, many of the names no longer are in my memory), but from what I can remember Kemintiri also had lvl 9 disciplines, and she wasnt even the oldest 4th generation Setite, much less the oldest 4th generation overall. And many many others.<br /> <br /> From what I remember of her. Kemintiri is still an ancient who is quite potent to begin with and would have max triats in some areas<br /> <br /> As for DC and Marvel and D&amp;D worlds, the presence of this beings do cause a MASSIVE impact in the world at large - to the point of sometimes having entire universes &quot;erased&quot; in those stories.<br /> <br /> I have not followed Marvel &amp; DC for quite some time due to all the meaningless reboots and I'm also acknowledging that I have changed and they have not really.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T10:50:56-07:00","id":1484373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484367#post1484367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does not bother me at all. Are we are equally athletic, charming, knowledgeable in all fields? No we are not and maybe charcters of the same generation and different ages would have their own strengths &amp; weaknesses</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that they don't need to have both a level 9 Discipline, as they may have focused on different things, Goratrix and Etrius aren't of same Gen and different ages. They're roughly the same age and have always been, as they're <i>exactly</i> the same age as vampires. They're Tremere's top students in life and undeath, and bitter rivals, this pair would definitely make sense to have similar stats, or at least XP values.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484367#post1484367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I remember of her. Kemintiri is still an ancient who is quite potent to begin with and would have max triats in some areas</div> </div> </div> </div>She's not the oldest 4th gen, but certainly figures among them. She's maybe the oldest to actually come to be in recorder history instead of outright pre-history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484367#post1484367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for DC and Marvel and D&amp;D worlds, the presence of this beings do cause a MASSIVE impact in the world at large - to the point of sometimes having entire universes &quot;erased&quot; in those stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the whole comparison is meaningless. The point in discussion depends on the premises of the setting, and here WoD has the complication of a premise of &quot;being like our world&quot;, all the time. Most comics have a somewhat similar premise, but they have far less attachment to it on the long run. D&amp;D uses fantasy worlds.<br /> <br /> This WoD premise is tricky and requires a lot of handwave, but I do think the MAD policy, plus focus on goals rather than on blowing things up for the giggles, is generally enough to hold it together in the face of super-powered NPCs better than most other handwaves we have to come up with in the game.<br /> <br /> Even the eventual NPC who wouldn't care, like a Nephandus, can still be held in place either by the intervention of others, or by their own understanding that going bananas won't really cause the lasting damage they want after someone comes to clean their shit afterwards. So even if you're a Nephandus Archmaster you won't squander your hard earned powers with a &quot;blaze of glory&quot; that won't even be remembered after a week or two (Rest in Pieces, Czar Vargo).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T10:05:06-07:00","id":1484427,"title":"","content":"Like I said. I don\u2019t follow DC or Marvel comics anymore due to the fact I have grown up and they haven\u2019t really. So I read more Manga and more adult oriented Image, Boom or Dynmaite studios. The only thing I can say about that is that the handbooks were funny. When every character was depicted as more potent then what was said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T18:11:50-07:00","id":1484463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That does not bother me at all. Are we are equally athletic, charming, knowledgeable in all fields? No we are not and maybe charcters of the same generation and different ages would have their own strengths &amp; weaknesses </div> </div> </div>I couldn't agree more. Characters are different and should be portrayed as such. Goratrix is a genius, so it makes a lot of sense to have him developing his powers at a much faster pace than others, besides, he has probably diablerized many cainites and many people tend to forget that diablerie gives A LOT of power. By the way, he already has officially Thaumaturgy 9 in his 1242 character sheet, which I think is quite fair. <br /> <br /> People tend to forget or don't like to think that we have many variables in real life, things like talent, luck (or destiny, whatever you want to call it) that makes all the difference. As geopolitics is my field specialty, I'd use the USA as a good example for some of these situations, like the Tremere winning war on various fronts, etc. Who would've thought a nation so young would become the most powerful country in the world in such a short timeframe? Imagine the possibilities the USA had, it's easy to think of so many possible terrible outcomes for them, but they were &quot;lucky&quot;, had their advantages and through a combination of factors became the most powerful nation in the world in less than 200 years of history. It's not really a hard exercise for the mind to imagine that the Tremere were both lucky and seized the opportunities they had, etc.<br /> <br /> I sincerely have a hard time understanding these folks who think time is the only relevant measure of power for a cainite. It isn't and never was. This premise is one of the most important pillars of what cainites and canite society works upon, the fact that you can steal power by consuming the soul of an ancient is one of the most important and relevant aspects of a vampire game. And here I'm not even taking into account what I said before about individual talents, sheer giftedness, etc. Even if you think every vampire is the same, i.e. if you think every cainite is created through the same <i>tabula rasa </i>concept, etc., the very existence of diablerie utterly destroy this notion that vampire power is only measured by age...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the whole comparison is meaningless. The point in discussion depends on the premises of the setting, and here WoD has the complication of a premise of &quot;being like our world&quot;, all the time. Most comics have a somewhat similar premise, but they have far less attachment to it on the long run. D&amp;D uses fantasy worlds. </div> </div> </div>I completely agree with that, this whole comparisson is pointless at this point of the discussion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T19:56:21-07:00","id":1484469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484463#post1484463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the very existence of diablerie utterly destroy this notion that vampire power is only measured by age...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not true. Not in a direct, objective sense. While it doesn't negate anything else in your post, this isn't a valid assertion of <u>fact</u>.<br /> <br /> There is no actual objective and official rule on this whatsoever. The few official books that ever dared to present something of this nature are somewhat obscure supplements presenting optional rules.<br /> <br /> What we factually have on the RAW is that Diablerie causes the following effects and them alone:<ul><li>Decrease of Generation by 1 if the victim was of lower generation, with further decrease <u>strictly at the ST's discretion</u>;<br /> \u200b</li> <li>Others are entitled a Perception roll to few unease at your presence for X* months;<br /> \u200b</li> <li>Aura marked by black stripes for X years (minimum 1 year);<br /> \u200b</li> <li>Self-Control/Instincts roll to avoid &quot;loosing control&quot; (for whatever that means);<br /> \u200b</li> <li>Regardless of benefits, it may cause addiction;<br /> \u200b</li> <li>You <b><u>may</u></b> receive extra Discipline levels <b><u>for a single scene</u></b> or longer, <u>at the ST's discretion</u>;<br /> \u200b</li> </ul>*X is Original Generation - Victim's Generation.<br /> <br /> And that's it. Anything that's at the ST's discretion may and should be considered unreliable at best in-game, so while some diablerists do experiment such benefits, there's no rhyme or reason to it that can remotely guarantee results. You may be 13th Gen, diablerize a 4th Gen Methuselah of 6 thousand years, and still get only to become 12th Gen and not a single second of extra powers out of the deal, and that's what you should indeed expect despite the chance of getting some extras.<br /> <br /> In this same section in the core it is said that <i><u><b>legends</b></u></i> talk about <b><u><i>sometimes</i></u></b> the act causing possession-like side effects that may be or may be not an actual possession, and may or may not lead to a permanent personality change. Some other books also claim that <b><u><i>legends</i></u></b> talk about greater, more permanent rewards from the act.<br /> <br /> Both claims are given in every official lore as unsubstantiated legends. There are only two case studies known to readers in greater detail, Saulot and Mithras, but those cases are also peppered with so many unknown factors and particular considerations that it isn't possible to draw definite conclusions (for starters, were they able to apply their powers while in Torpor? They're both masters in Disciplines that are geared to cause the effects saw in their Assailant-Victims).<br /> <br /> My point here is to remind you that, while greater rewards from Diablerie are a popular approach that many, many tables use and the lore somewhat accepts as a possibility, it is <b><u>not</u></b> an official fact of the setting for more objective, house-rule agnostic discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  add underline 06-19-2022, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T21:17:58-07:00","id":1484472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484469#post1484469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What we factually have on the RAW is that Diablerie causes the following effects and them alone:<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> My point here is to remind you that, while greater rewards from Diablerie are a popular approach that many, many tables use and the lore somewhat accepts as a possibility, it is <b><u>not</u></b> an official fact of the setting for more objective, house-rule agnostic discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget the aggressor, dubbed the diablerist, automatically loses some of its Humanity, usually -1 Humanity for this cannibalistic act<br /> Or more if you are high enough<br /> Even Road/Way-walkers are not safe, of course its up to interpretation of the given set of moral rules, but most of them are not really keen on the idea of such horrible deed<br /> Some requires it, but thats another can of worms<br /> The whole idea comes from the 1985 Anna Rice Novel, The Vampire Lestat and the 1988 The Queen of the Damned, where Mekare kills Akasha by severing her head and consumse her brain and heart.<br /> Anyhow, Diableie is more like a forbidden drug, it is said to bestow the greatest pleasure imaginable to the diablerist, greater than the Kiss. But even this is a bit apocrifical<br /> It could lead a premature Thirst of Ages, but that one is not for power, just a step up on the food chain; like Animals barely sustanied a vampire compared to human, with enough time, human blood became useless, you need stronger, more potent stuf, with age you became the Predator of the Predators, your own kind. Mind you that is purely for feeding, not power and you don't need to consume the soul<br /> Diableie is feared, with a reason, but in reality, its not the worse of the way to go<br /> Vampires are damned after all, tho' there are no evidence, what exactly awaits you after Final Death... sometimes you became a wraith ,sometimes just gone till someone summons your suposedly damned soul that should belong in a Hell (tho it is a damaged proerity, a &quot;living&quot; vampire is more usefull than a tattered soul of a dead one for an old school demon) <br /> Even if the diablerie totally consumes your soul and you literally case to exist, oblivion is better then eternity in Hell - at laeast for some, in Hell you always have some glimmer of hope, you will escape. <br /> Sorry, where was I? Tend to wander away on my trail of toughts during conversations<br /> Diablerie!<br /> Nothing is actually sure, like how monteparnas said; power boost, generation, etc<br /> The sure thing is the -1 Humanity, stained soul and the fact, its better than the Kiss... the rest is very very very optional rules wise, and in game, filled wiht more legends and superstitions than the Golconda","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T21:41:09-07:00","id":1484474,"title":"","content":"Don't you get haunted by the voices of the Vampire consumed by Diablerie? <br /> <br /> Or is that just in Requiem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T05:25:33-07:00","id":1484503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484472#post1484472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget the aggressor, dubbed the diablerist, automatically loses some of its Humanity, usually -1 Humanity for this cannibalistic act<br /> Or more if you are high enough</div> </div> </div> </div>Curiously, despite writing that it was those effects alone, I was totally, completely, 100% sure I was forgetting something, no much, but one thing.<br /> <br /> Yeah, you lose 1 Humanity + whatever loss the crime would entail anyway (usually murder). And again, more at the ST's discretion, same observation applied, so even it being murder you're only guaranteed the -1 Humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484472#post1484472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">filled wiht more legends and superstitions than the Golconda</div> </div> </div> </div>Another nice curiosity, that's completely true. While most table apply more bonuses for Diablerie and treat Golconda as an impossible undertaking, we actually have far more concrete data and rules on Golconda in the official lore than in what happens when you eat a &quot;soul&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484474#post1484474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you get haunted by the voices of the Vampire consumed by Diablerie?<br /> <br /> Or is that just in Requiem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just Requiem, although the idea was present in Masquerade as this legend that so many people assume as true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T12:40:56-07:00","id":1484536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is no actual objective and official rule on this whatsoever. The few official books that ever dared to present something of this nature are somewhat obscure supplements presenting optional rules. </div> </div> </div>It's not stated explicitly in the rules of core books (most likely to curb players from acquiring too much power from it), but it's always been implied it's the case in the metaplot of the setting. You absorb the soul of another cainite, and through it all his powers, etc, there are many rituals and combinations of disciplines that use this in their flavour text and increase the benefit of the act, etc. The fact that the core books didn't bother to provide good or interesting rules for what happens in the meta is another matter entirely. The only book that I can remember now that provides actual (good) rules to Diablerie is The Guide to the Tall'Mahe'Ra and at least there one find rules for acquiring disciplines and powers from it and the possibility of losing control to the one diablerized, like what happened in the diablerie of Saulot and Mithras. Also &quot;obscure supmements&quot; is a very subjective term, I feel, with all due respect, that here you're just being a &quot;rules lawyer&quot; and not adding much to the discussion, only adding unnecessary possible complications that only serve to dilute what I said, in other words, it looks like provocation. Whatever...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The whole idea comes from the 1985 Anna Rice Novel </div> </div> </div>The &quot;whole idea&quot; comes from the very concept of Cannibalism, only imported to the world of vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 06-20-2022, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T23:56:42-07:00","id":1484585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484536#post1484536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not stated explicitly in the rules of core books (most likely to curb players from acquiring too much power from it), but it's always been implied it's the case in the metaplot of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without caveats. It has always been implied that the possibility exists, yet couldn't be proven. So as much as it has been implied to happen in some cases, it has also been implied that it does not happen every time (as it is also implied that Diablerie happens with some frequency between not so distant vampires, like a Neophyte getting another Neophyte or young Acilla 1 or 2 Generations lower) and that neither benefits or drawbacks can be predicted with any reliability, or even be confirmed to exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484536#post1484536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also &quot;obscure supmements&quot; is a very subjective term</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, but it is relevant to determine how likely a concept is to be assumed as standard versus as an exception. There's a lot of difference on inferring implications for something being true on about half the books, only in the core, or only in one supplement, specially if this supplement relates to a more strict theme.<br /> <br /> Virtually all books in the history of the setting assuming as default that any character actually committing Diablerie won't face further effects unless the ST wants to, and usually that such effects will be temporary if they happen at all. That includes core books, Player Guides, Storyteller Companions, and every other book meant to be a staple on mechanics or cover a broad aspect of the game.<br /> <br /> There are two or three exceptions, two of them being about the Tal'Mahe'Ra, which I am confident to say to be a concept of limited scope in the setting (not talking about the scope of the organization itself, which is gigantic). It can hardly be considered that the implied intent is that those books are the ones telling the official stance on the matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484536#post1484536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel, with all due respect, that here you're just being a &quot;rules lawyer&quot; and not adding much to the discussion, only adding unnecessary possible complications that only serve to dilute what I said, in other words, it looks like provocation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not my intention, I guarantee you.<br /> <br /> What you said, and that I responded to, was that the idea of Diablerie goes against the notion of power coming from age.<br /> <br /> And what I mean by all this is that by no means this is the intended theme of the setting. Behind those rules is a theme, and by making the standard rules give you little in the way of direct power when lowering your Generation (or being Embraced into a low Generation to begin with), the game is playing <i>directly</i> into the notion of the Power of the Ages, not against it. It is a central theme on itself, frequently repeated, either with or without association to Generation.<br /> <br /> The game isn't binary on this, and the legends are there both to make Diablerie more tempting and give the ST the power to tweak those themes in their game, but as a rule of thumb the seizing of this power by the young is an exception, not the rule. The young can go a long way on their own or through Diablerie, but only age will give you mastery. Exceptions like the Tremere happen, but they're that, the exception, and usually go hand in hand with other special circumstances (a House of Awakened Mages and a family that has practiced Necromancy for millennia aren't exactly your standard fare for new vampires).<br /> <br /> Can you apply those ideas and throw away the theme of power tied to time? Certainly. But you can't say this is RAI, the setting is built around this trope and the rules are how they are by design.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484536#post1484536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;whole idea&quot; comes from the very concept of Cannibalism, only imported to the world of vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, nonetheless.<br /> <br /> Even eating meat comes with traditions all over the world about gaining the strength of the animals you eat. That's not a new concept.<br /> <br /> But on a more specific note, IIRC someone once admitted that this actually came to VtM specifically from Highlander. There's a thred about that somewhere in the forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T10:59:49-07:00","id":1484625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not without caveats. It has always been implied that the possibility exists, yet couldn't be proven. So as much as it has been implied to happen in some cases, it has also been implied that it does not happen every time (as it is also implied that Diablerie happens with some frequency between not so distant vampires, like a Neophyte getting another Neophyte or young Acilla 1 or 2 Generations lower) and that neither benefits or drawbacks can be predicted with any reliability, or even be confirmed to exist. </div> </div> </div>I agree in the point that it gives the ST freedom to allow or not to allow cainites (in this case, specifically the players) to acquire power through diablerie(btw VTM gives A LOT of freedom to ST in basically everything, as a friend of mine once put it, in vampire one cannot even be sure about how is damage or soak handled, as it varies according to the book and, naturally, the ST), in this case I mean &quot;true power&quot;, in the sense of stealing powers like the rules written in the guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra gives (certainly the best set of rules released for diablerie in the history of the game, as it represents very well, what &quot;we feel&quot; in the subtext of the metaplot). In my opinion, they only didn't conveyd it completely to the rules in the core books (giving instead, &quot;half-rewards&quot; in the form of temporary disciplines and the possibility of some being permanent, cheaper to buy or at the very least giving access to disciplines the cainite didn't know before, etc) in order to not give &quot;way too big of a reward&quot; and somehow curb players' &quot;powerplay&quot;, so to speak (I'm not sure if I'm being clear here, I'm really tired and English isn't even my second language lol). But as I said, it's has always being implied somehow as a theme and we can see many examples of such famous diablerists who suddenly acquired a lot of power in short amount of time due to diablerie, or whose &quot;largest share of power&quot; was acquired from diablerie in the description of the character's story, etc , e.g. Monty (classic example, as I don't want to focus on the Tremere), Anatole, Tariq, etc. Even though Anatole doesn't have a really impressive character sheet, the variety of powers he has is easily implied to come from diablerie. Also, as I said, there are many rituals and combinations of disciplines that use the theme and reinforces it, Blade of the Forbidden Flower (from Blood Magic) is probably the one that uses it best, as it basically allows the vampire to dieablerize another cainite and, but instead of absorbing himself the powers of the cainite, allows him to place these powers into a weapon, Drink the Mind (from Guide to the Low Clans) is another that comes to mind, as it's stated in the diablerie rules that diablerie doesn't give access to knowledge and Blood Sorcery, this combination of disciplines, basically allows the cainite to circumvent it and allow the cainite to absorb skills and knowledge and as such, basically gives the player a &quot;legal precedent&quot; to steal Blood Magic from his diablerized victims. So, as I said, it's a very strong theme in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even eating meat comes with traditions all over the world about gaining the strength of the animals you eat. That's not a new concept. </div> </div> </div>True, it's definitely not a new concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But on a more specific note, IIRC someone once admitted that this actually came to VtM specifically from Highlander. There's a thred about that somewhere in the forums. </div> </div> </div>That's quite interesting, I wish I had the source. It seems the concept in both worlds is very similar and Highlander certainly had a strong influence in VTM. Very interesting indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 06-21-2022, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T23:10:28-07:00","id":1484672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483112-powerful-methuselah-or-antedilluvian-imposing-his-will-on-camarilla?p=1484625#post1484625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, they only didn't conveyd it completely to the rules in the core books (giving instead, &quot;half-rewards&quot; in the form of temporary disciplines and the possibility of some being permanent, cheaper to buy or at the very least giving access to disciplines the cainite didn't know before, etc) in order to not give &quot;way too big of a reward&quot; and somehow curb players' &quot;powerplay&quot;, so to speak</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the crux of the matter: I'm not convinced this was the intention, or at least not to this extent and not exclusively (and it can't be conclusively decided from the rules alone, in neither direction). There is a theme of Power of Age, and it partially trumps the theme of stealing power through consumption, which is the reason one can't be considered decidedly more canon. This is even more relevant if we take the <i>Highlander</i> inspiration seriously, which would make the core rules similar to the first movie's Quickening and basically have those other options as based on the Quickening in the series and other movies (with the whole thing being less a soul steal and more of a Dark Quickening). But without the source, let's just keep this as a possible middle ground interpretation.<br /> <br /> We can discuss at length what stealing only Generation means anyway. Or stealing Generation plus the capacity to develop Disciplines without further help other than XP. The fact is that on the long run, and if the game didn't had high level stats so overpriced, this would be enough for a huge advantage anyway without giving all the goodies at once, which may cover more of what we see in the lore than it seems at first. For example, there's no indication that the Tremere or that Augustus Giovanni got any additional powers from Diablerie as they were formidable people already and very advanced on the kind of thing that would become their main powers even before undeath.<br /> <br /> In the end, the game has many characters that committed Diablerie and achieved considerable power, but few that we can say for sure that there's a tight link between the two things, and even less certainty that it bypassed any of the many option that we would describe as &quot;increasing traits through XP&quot;. Add to it the possible secrets those characters hold, and the only, single character that we have that can be objectively pointed to as having absorbed permanent stats was Monty.<br /> <br /> And rituals, Disciplines and other interventions have the problem of being exactly that: interventions. They're by definition not the default state of a character and not how most in the setting will have it. And it is hard to say which stance their existence reinforce as the intention of the game as a whole. Is this a sign that any character with enough dedication can acquire the means to obtain greater powers? Or does that indicates that the one with this power is a &quot;cheater&quot; of sorts, a threat to the world at large for its ability to bypass the limitations that are meant to be? Do they tell about how the authors wanted the setting to be, or are meant to explain exceptions not intended to become rules?<br /> <br /> Even the Tremere offer us a hint: most of the clan committed Diablerie at the time wantonly, and the Inner Circle did it to Elders and Methuselah. Yet we hardly if ever have news of them showing many signs of those transfers having occurred, neither personality nor power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}